UPDATE comments c SET body = v.body, parent_comment_id = v.parent, created_at = v.ts FROM (VALUES
  ('68c917c5-4dcd-4672-afad-f21451c16f2c'::uuid, 'Quick follow-up to my post: I''ll keep a running list of what we learn about global scenario here. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for cyber law.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-30T02:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2231676d-6994-4a4a-88ac-87ed7dac9f75'::uuid, 'I skimmed the paper last week, and the framing of global scenario is the part I would discuss first. A colleague''s project on cyber law hit the same issue with global scenario. Is there a public dataset we could use to test global scenario ourselves?', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-05T03:14:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e12d2a2e-c73f-4ae5-adfd-ea2e669bf3a2'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Varun: the evidence for global scenario is thinner than it looks. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for cyber law. Last semester''s reading group went through “Cyber Law”, and most of the debate centred on global scenario.', '2231676d-6994-4a4a-88ac-87ed7dac9f75'::uuid, '2026-09-08T01:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('1050fb6c-496c-4b71-bd93-74bce2b58fe3'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of global scenario. For context, the synthetic biology literature has been debating a very similar question for some time.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-08T23:17:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a051fc36-fa4d-4691-9713-feb4a14b5f6d'::uuid, 'If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-31T06:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('00065343-af38-47ef-b32e-958add2e8d5e'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on cyber law. It would help to state the assumptions behind global scenario formally and check which of them actually hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-06T01:39:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('90cabebb-da21-41e3-a3bc-5df9efece8ef'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on cyber law. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude. How does this compare with last year''s work on digital humanities?', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-05T04:54:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('1544ba31-5026-44d3-8e9f-9e15aa42dbbb'::uuid, 'Do the authors say anything about computational cost for global scenario?', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-09T11:16:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7f0aeab9-40ca-461f-a7d6-1d316bb60d6e'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying protein folding in practice. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from chaperones versus simply more tuning. Is there a public dataset we could use to test catalyzing protein folding ourselves? Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-06T00:14:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ab231189-2db4-4b10-9286-abfce43b2017'::uuid, 'Omkar, could you say more about how you handled catalyzing protein folding? It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics.', '7f0aeab9-40ca-461f-a7d6-1d316bb60d6e'::uuid, '2026-10-06T02:54:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f039f250-cba1-4ec7-bb8c-ed14b27d6c24'::uuid, 'Did you check how it performs when the input around chaperones is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-04T16:37:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('16daa068-bff6-47e3-8b49-4e9a6df63b38'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. The recent papers in our library on synthetic biology would make a good companion read. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around protein folding easier to trust.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-04T09:10:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('00170b65-d715-4c62-bc9b-25345b7eff31'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on protein folding. Did you check how it performs when the input around chaperones is noisy or partially missing? Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-30T18:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('004d47d5-e050-4870-b93f-c84acddbb6c8'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on graph neural networks for a while, so I''m glad it came up. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-04T21:17:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e1ee50c6-8d77-485b-9b2b-725613404c57'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the auto-gnn question deserves more attention than it gets. Related reading: surveys on bioinformatics cover the background on neural architecture search nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-08T14:16:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f5d3e7fa-cc7c-48b1-9ad8-428c0d062edc'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the auto-gnn piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. The social context of graph neural networks is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for graph neural networks.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-11T09:17:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('1521f7b9-c7fd-450c-88ec-b247dfaa3ed1'::uuid, 'Thanks Karthik, this is exactly the feedback I was hoping for. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for graph neural networks?', 'e1ee50c6-8d77-485b-9b2b-725613404c57'::uuid, '2026-10-11T00:11:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('36df945c-b7a9-4813-8705-a2c3fd6633cc'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Aarav: the evidence for auto-gnn is thinner than it looks. The recent papers in our library on protein folding would make a good companion read.', 'f5d3e7fa-cc7c-48b1-9ad8-428c0d062edc'::uuid, '2026-10-12T06:54:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4d689ccd-f058-4666-af0a-2d57920e47e6'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of bioinformatics keeps coming up in our seminars. How does this compare with last year''s work on data privacy law? The recent papers in our library on data privacy law would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-09T11:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('26138098-54e9-4736-9e0a-940b0b51163a'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a mathematical point of view. I would like to see a simple analytical baseline for bioinformatics before trusting the more elaborate method.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-03T00:22:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ee52428a-ce01-49ec-bceb-01754abd41f9'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying bioinformatics in practice. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for bioinformatics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-11T08:42:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f7375f4a-bc28-4535-8ac3-6877c3339c24'::uuid, 'That is a fair summary, Deepak, but one detail about bioinformatics is missing.', '26138098-54e9-4736-9e0a-940b0b51163a'::uuid, '2026-06-03T21:10:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0055fd58-145c-400c-8cca-78e3bf34771d'::uuid, 'I skimmed the paper last week, and the framing of bioinformatics is the part I would discuss first. The biological interpretation of bioinformatics is where I would be most careful. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around bioinformatics easier to trust. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-08T19:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ed1ee4f1-6964-4fa8-bb06-2dd5b9aa25ed'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of the paper is less the headline number and more how it handles bioinformatics. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-09T10:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ea41366c-8ab1-4532-8cc3-2bb48b0eb9d5'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of bioinformatics keeps coming up in our seminars. For context, the intellectual property literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-05T02:39:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ae8d7e02-d6f7-4092-9149-fa2a25e7499d'::uuid, 'Good point, Gaurav; I had not considered that angle on bioinformatics.', 'ea41366c-8ab1-4532-8cc3-2bb48b0eb9d5'::uuid, '2026-07-05T21:14:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0aea69f3-f86a-47cb-ac5d-148ed8897c10'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. We reproduced part of this for bioinformatics and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the bioinformatics results hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-02T13:56:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('00590d9c-2f7e-4aa3-8a09-ac29243a0cad'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the bioinformatics question deserves more attention than it gets. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for bioinformatics? This connects to the work on digital humanities, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-09T17:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c9136cbf-97ea-4927-9d21-c6123f84f66a'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on bioinformatics. There is a useful parallel with sustainable finance, where the role of bioinformatics is comparable. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-13T11:52:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('358c5dc0-0559-4c8c-8237-433d8b86b525'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the bangladesh s data privacy piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-23T03:43:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('87d940d6-0812-49f6-8f4a-5cebcafcfe88'::uuid, 'Thanks Pallavi, that clarifies the bangladesh s data privacy part for me.', '358c5dc0-0559-4c8c-8237-433d8b86b525'::uuid, '2026-08-24T21:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('549b7b57-e6bc-4db1-9394-d0f293a4b016'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the bangladesh s data privacy piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? A colleague''s project on data privacy law hit the same issue with bangladesh s data privacy.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-25T00:37:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('64d9f2a4-be62-47b0-8432-a2a4d489f796'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. This connects to the work on cyber law, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-21T17:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('005a12f4-8a07-48df-95b1-d1503199105d'::uuid, 'Agreed with Prakash on the main point. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for data privacy law? The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of analysis.', '549b7b57-e6bc-4db1-9394-d0f293a4b016'::uuid, '2026-08-27T04:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5b153fd8-4b35-4004-9ed2-4c16858b4f80'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around bangladesh s data privacy is easy to underestimate. One option is to run a small ablation on analysis and share the numbers with the group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-24T09:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('007a7fe6-aa3a-4a59-bf25-c5af978fde20'::uuid, 'Saving this; the businesses angle is useful.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-31T14:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('11b076a0-7493-47d1-9cb7-e2dba0203533'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on sustainable finance for a while, so I''m glad it came up. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding management challenges. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-03T17:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('1318b09d-0654-459c-b81d-98316e4b80f4'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for sustainable finance. Did you check how it performs when the input around management challenges is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-31T09:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4e14e58b-d598-46c8-a37e-fdcf7176bdf7'::uuid, 'Agreed; this is worth benchmarking properly.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-09T04:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5777648c-180f-4f0a-b6df-f0b21cf0bfd3'::uuid, 'Helpful context, Gaurav. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the sustainable finance results hold.', '1318b09d-0654-459c-b81d-98316e4b80f4'::uuid, '2026-08-01T11:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c2445e75-6591-4be1-967e-a1e10844bfc2'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. A leaderboard number alone will not tell us whether work on wireless sensor networks is robust enough for deployment. Did you check how it performs when the input around energy sustainability is noisy or partially missing? Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-06T07:49:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('008ca4d9-3391-413d-a74a-897aabcdc02e'::uuid, 'One option is to run a small ablation on energy sustainability and share the numbers with the group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-03T12:08:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7b723b50-b5bf-40e2-b910-f9badf813033'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Bhavana: the evidence for analytical is thinner than it looks.', '008ca4d9-3391-413d-a74a-897aabcdc02e'::uuid, '2026-11-05T16:10:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c63393a7-530e-4677-8b40-8b58376514b5'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Neha. It would be worth asking whose perspective is missing from the data behind energy sustainability. Is there a public dataset we could use to test analytical ourselves? Happy to share my notes if that helps.', 'c2445e75-6591-4be1-967e-a1e10844bfc2'::uuid, '2026-11-08T14:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('68acac2b-98e9-4cda-b2e0-ab7631a96202'::uuid, 'Worth a closer look when we plan the next wireless sensor networks project.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-02T18:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('008dd1cb-37e9-4cc8-998f-0ec683908bdd'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. The recent papers in our library on embedded systems would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-29T10:48:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a0cd5c32-790c-47fb-a983-ce1fa0d53cf2'::uuid, 'Useful pointer, thank you.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-22T00:01:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0399024a-b57f-4264-8d54-6eaec3f8de2c'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Intellectual Property” is a useful lens on intellectual property. On our side the intellectual property step was the bottleneck, not the main method.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-02T04:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4c72e4f4-826d-466c-b888-f301b209cab2'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. I would add a humanities lens: how research on intellectual property is framed and interpreted matters as much as the technical result. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-27T16:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('00aeb65c-7c6a-4c64-9e7b-cad5cd9b80e4'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “A review of convolutional neural networks in computer vision” is less the headline number and more how it handles convolutional neural networks. Related reading: surveys on cyber law cover the background on convolutional neural networks nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-02T12:56:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a1700a29-5290-441e-a3d2-8daa64638334'::uuid, 'How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-09T06:58:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f9e40783-57aa-443a-9155-221d69632184'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the convolutional neural networks piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. This connects to the work on bioinformatics, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-02T07:56:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2f1607cc-05b1-426c-a659-7403bbd4d3ae'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the convolutional neural networks piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for computer vision. From an engineering angle, I would want to see how computer vision behaves under distribution shift before relying on it.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-08T15:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('6a224dab-1516-4af6-ac38-e1786fe001d5'::uuid, 'I skimmed the paper last week, and the framing of convolutional neural networks is the part I would discuss first. Related reading: surveys on synthetic biology cover the background on convolutional neural networks nicely. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for convolutional neural networks? Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-03T19:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('09b05bc8-1764-4144-8c66-524b07c2d9c1'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Related reading: surveys on consumer behavior cover the background on wireless sensor networks nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-19T22:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('072919e3-0262-4111-9b90-460b1a49efb0'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Wireless Sensor Networks” is less the headline number and more how it handles wireless sensor networks. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the wireless sensor networks results? Public-facing claims about wireless sensor networks deserve careful wording, since non-specialists will read them very differently.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-18T14:20:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('00b05530-7feb-4d69-8a2e-99b50dd19414'::uuid, 'Solid point, and well put.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-28T13:34:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('66fecf96-04db-4614-8ca6-307789997d51'::uuid, 'That is a fair summary, Mallika, but one detail about wireless sensor networks is missing. There is a useful parallel with computer vision, where the role of wireless sensor networks is comparable. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics. I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', '09b05bc8-1764-4144-8c66-524b07c2d9c1'::uuid, '2026-06-22T13:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b355a15a-6c6d-4212-b063-b70c55b8f532'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Wireless Sensor Networks” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about wireless sensor networks in the wild. Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-20T05:09:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('13814cfc-b651-4460-b749-6ada0b3851dd'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Consider tracking g-quadruplexes rescuing protein folding separately so that regressions are easier to spot.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-14T16:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('27590b30-c1e9-4422-bbeb-f9f92a7fbe09'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Aditi. A colleague''s project on protein folding hit the same issue with g-quadruplexes rescuing protein folding.', '13814cfc-b651-4460-b749-6ada0b3851dd'::uuid, '2026-10-17T10:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d5c4df1e-3639-4750-add4-d7274d5ea152'::uuid, 'Appreciate the pointers, Aditi; I will try that on my next run. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split. There is a useful parallel with graph neural networks, where the role of g-quadruplexes rescuing protein folding is comparable. Happy to share my notes if that helps.', '13814cfc-b651-4460-b749-6ada0b3851dd'::uuid, '2026-10-14T18:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('00bdf2d6-b786-435c-9e6c-f8c97c4474f2'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Aditya: the evidence for g-quadruplexes rescuing protein folding is thinner than it looks.', '27590b30-c1e9-4422-bbeb-f9f92a7fbe09'::uuid, '2026-10-17T16:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f02d0e5b-e617-42a2-a02a-a1c8a7a9b39d'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. On our side the g-quadruplexes rescuing protein folding step was the bottleneck, not the main method. There is a useful parallel with large language models, where the role of g-quadruplexes rescuing protein folding is comparable.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-10T00:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b37201ea-4cd8-49e5-b234-a656f2e9cf96'::uuid, 'I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about data mining in the wild.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-09T01:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('00be8076-972f-4ba4-8e02-3179cdb7eeed'::uuid, 'I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper.', NULL::uuid, '2026-05-31T19:36:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('1776ce73-fc16-4c48-8d38-4ad8a0137897'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the data mining piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around data mining easier to trust. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from fintech adoption; the overlap with data mining looks real. Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-09T07:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('aa95ec77-cca6-4c4f-beef-a22d3af185dc'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. When we tried a similar setup for data mining, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did. Did you check how it performs when the input around data mining is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-07T05:27:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('13051378-9d4e-42f1-8451-e3d87a899298'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. When we tried a similar setup for protein folding, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-08T23:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('06bfd6de-f6ac-4b9e-978e-ee1fcecb051c'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Is Water the Engine of Protein Folding?” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. Did you check how it performs when the input around protein folding is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-10T17:16:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
