  ('01354088-d330-4056-8205-4712c6cb5c58'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Kavya.', 'cdc7f3c6-c197-49eb-9eef-77ad69ce4279'::uuid, '2026-06-01T09:17:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('01812f32-8878-437a-ba29-70bf6298a100'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of protein folding keeps coming up in our seminars. Adoption is usually limited by process and incentives, so any plan to adopt protein folding needs a realistic rollout story. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the protein folding results hold. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-28T16:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0199821b-174c-4112-8c4b-2d3969ab6bb0'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. I would add a humanities lens: how research on cognitive psychology is framed and interpreted matters as much as the technical result.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-07T19:27:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fcc8d91d-e49f-4cb1-b369-5e8126b17276'::uuid, 'Prakash, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around cognitive psychology easier to trust.', '0199821b-174c-4112-8c4b-2d3969ab6bb0'::uuid, '2026-09-10T16:27:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f8046a2b-d905-4a8d-b1ce-a70480f4be8c'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of the paper is less the headline number and more how it handles history. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding scripts.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-11T05:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a8bdaa51-6bff-4f40-b5f5-21b84c0239bf'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Scripts in the History of AI and Cognitive Psychology” is less the headline number and more how it handles scripts. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-13T06:26:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('033d0dda-d436-4c66-9bd9-7f69d72ee39f'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “3Digital Humanities and/as Media Studies” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-31T21:16:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
