  ('2f1da319-508e-47ed-84e7-6bc01445ae8b'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on consumer behavior for a while, so I''m glad it came up. How does this compare with last year''s work on synthetic biology? A cleaner experiment might isolate voice assistant recommendations and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-03T12:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f67735fd-f57c-4799-a469-aeff618e457a'::uuid, 'Agreed with Aishwarya on the main point. Last semester''s reading group went through the paper, and most of the debate centred on voice assistant recommendations.', '2f1da319-508e-47ed-84e7-6bc01445ae8b'::uuid, '2026-10-03T23:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('aed57783-00a7-4451-af3e-a6fd911f79aa'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Graph Neural Networks for Recommender System” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. Did you check how it performs when the input around recommender system is noisy or partially missing? It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-06T16:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('026f9f62-8296-4be6-b5e9-a723dbc5bd0a'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on graph neural networks. A colleague''s project on graph neural networks hit the same issue with recommender system. If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-12T17:50:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bbe4c55f-7d48-4bb2-8c4e-dcfe1419d720'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the recommender system piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. A cleaner experiment might isolate recommender system and keep everything else fixed. I would flag the privacy and public-policy implications of recommender system before anyone builds on it.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-08T15:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('33205291-833d-440b-889a-0466a15f9cc3'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Embedded System and Software” is less the headline number and more how it handles embedded system. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-05-24T21:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ce150610-ef84-4716-a227-587716463b94'::uuid, 'Building on Kavya''s comment, the software assumption matters a lot here. From a statistical point of view, I would want to see uncertainty estimates around the embedded systems results, not only point values.', '33205291-833d-440b-889a-0466a15f9cc3'::uuid, '2026-05-25T11:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9d121ecf-5ae6-4855-bbab-b643e74348dd'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of embedded systems keeps coming up in our seminars. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of software.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-03T15:39:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('02b17bd6-4415-4d59-9376-c417a47694dd'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the software piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about embedded systems are to small changes in the data. For context, the digital humanities literature has been debating a very similar question for some time.', NULL::uuid, '2026-05-30T01:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fb955153-5da5-4ae2-af9a-e4d03df445a4'::uuid, 'Do the authors say anything about computational cost for understand GPT-?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-11T20:37:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('02cc72cb-c251-43ba-a889-ffb9c0def8e9'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying cognitive psychology in practice. It would be worth asking whose perspective is missing from the data behind understand GPT-.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-18T00:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('56203ad7-918f-47ef-81fc-32fb3fa723f5'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. Liability and transparency around cognitive psychology are still unsettled, and this paper does not address them.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-20T23:41:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('46f8f2b3-c70c-4b7b-b178-67899fbba493'::uuid, 'Thanks for pushing on this, Radhika; I''ll report back once I have numbers for understand GPT-. There is a useful parallel with synthetic biology, where the role of understand GPT- is comparable. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the understand GPT- results?', '02cc72cb-c251-43ba-a889-ffb9c0def8e9'::uuid, '2026-10-18T02:13:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3c1494d7-8238-4e4e-b2be-2c8004ddbd3a'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on cognitive psychology. A cleaner experiment might isolate understand GPT- and keep everything else fixed. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-18T21:07:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('02f9cc21-4d5f-4a7c-8caf-7d0ac1fac9ac'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on artificial intelligence regulation for a while, so I''m glad it came up. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the important role results?', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-02T04:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
