  ('fe8fe119-d1f8-4668-a02f-c92d1f987f4b'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around librarianship is easy to underestimate. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of librarianship. How does this compare with last year''s work on sustainable finance?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-13T10:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5a99487d-d9be-41d1-8add-df15606c4634'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around librarianship is easy to underestimate. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split. Our lab has been collecting notes on librarianship; the picture is more nuanced than the abstract suggests. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-12T09:46:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('03c64d6c-2d65-46ae-ae32-dd248b1b60d8'::uuid, 'Helpful context, Prakash. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from librarianship versus simply more tuning.', 'c9651166-ee63-4d98-baab-1a1fa35d7160'::uuid, '2026-06-19T17:00:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('aa1b8645-4e0a-4dee-9b51-abff9b6dfb0b'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Prakash. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from librarianship versus simply more tuning. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one?', 'c9651166-ee63-4d98-baab-1a1fa35d7160'::uuid, '2026-06-22T04:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('71d3e802-6bee-4526-8f8b-027d8cb02a97'::uuid, 'Worth a closer look when we plan the next artificial intelligence regulation project.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-18T06:14:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('32f9d105-4ddd-4542-8071-c42a5480f1b1'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around justice is easy to underestimate. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the artificial intelligence regulation results hold. I would add a humanities lens: how research on artificial intelligence regulation is framed and interpreted matters as much as the technical result.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-09T12:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('18ba66cf-694d-405d-9441-50f53b38ed6e'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. Consider tracking algorithmic regulation separately so that regressions are easier to spot.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-16T16:33:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4c47cf78-98bc-4360-999c-239243768bf5'::uuid, 'Prakash, that matches my experience too. Our lab has been collecting notes on justice; the picture is more nuanced than the abstract suggests. Liability and transparency around artificial intelligence regulation are still unsettled, and this paper does not address them. Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', '32f9d105-4ddd-4542-8071-c42a5480f1b1'::uuid, '2026-06-12T01:14:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('03cdf7e6-3c1c-4cb6-be24-52ca3ea413da'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the labor competitiveness question deserves more attention than it gets. Did you check how it performs when the input around justice is noisy or partially missing? There is a useful parallel with intellectual property, where the role of algorithmic regulation is comparable. Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-17T20:07:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('52dbbf76-8653-41b2-b3d7-aae7e0cba4a3'::uuid, 'Swati, could you say more about how you handled justice? Related reading: surveys on large language models cover the background on labor competitiveness nicely. Consider tracking algorithmic regulation separately so that regressions are easier to spot.', '03cdf7e6-3c1c-4cb6-be24-52ca3ea413da'::uuid, '2026-06-18T05:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('53ec0e7c-56ed-448f-aa04-b8599faff5e7'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. In our group we used labor competitiveness on a small artificial intelligence regulation dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent. There is a useful parallel with intellectual property, where the role of algorithmic regulation is comparable. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-17T04:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('30c7006a-7738-4662-9fd5-003a27a4bc2b'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying data privacy law in practice. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input. I would add a humanities lens: how research on data privacy law is framed and interpreted matters as much as the technical result.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-29T09:08:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2d0f7b89-8056-4c7b-84f5-b5b1e79ed745'::uuid, 'Good point, Varun; I had not considered that angle on data privacy law. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for international data privacy law? Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split. I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', '30c7006a-7738-4662-9fd5-003a27a4bc2b'::uuid, '2026-10-01T06:02:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
