  ('ae1c3246-58ce-4002-af29-26231e8960e6'::uuid, 'Building on Deepak''s comment, the opportunities assumption matters a lot here. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding foundation models.', '0407587d-3c7c-4f2e-b8ac-2c6356351045'::uuid, '2026-10-13T10:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dc069082-8112-43ce-aa9e-dffbfa7bc993'::uuid, 'Good question. I read the paper a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the opportunities results?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-15T21:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('faf4f6e6-3079-4c70-89a2-d0330cf9eb93'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Progress and opportunities of foundation models in bioinformatics” is less the headline number and more how it handles foundation models. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say fintech adoption? Last semester''s reading group went through “Progress and opportunities of foundation models in bioinformatics”, and most of the debate centred on progress. I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-06T23:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ccd1e3dc-3798-47d3-ab3d-4c62d8d7f780'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the data privacy laws piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. Related reading: surveys on supply chain analytics cover the background on united states nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-22T00:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
