  ('58c48b1a-34a4-4a18-bcb2-83cec35e7ecf'::uuid, 'Agreed with Suresh on the main point. For context, the media studies literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. How does this compare with last year''s work on media studies?', '5c12e787-53e1-4454-aa99-d79304088583'::uuid, '2026-07-03T05:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b0507343-6a9e-4dd6-91f8-78343291af93'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on cyber law for a while, so I''m glad it came up. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one? I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-03T06:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('075d2bc0-134a-461f-b8d6-6c3f5db1b6d9'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Tarun. Related reading: surveys on media studies cover the background on cyber laws nicely.', 'f5cd6291-83c8-4927-b8df-dd2140844eb6'::uuid, '2026-07-12T13:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('31d9bc8b-817b-4c71-8eef-ef7c8a4b17a9'::uuid, 'Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-23T18:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
