  ('ca8399bc-573c-4179-ba97-1b9ac2bc8ea6'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Signal Processing” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for signal processing.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-05T18:23:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d151c903-c3a4-4778-903c-3994d14049b8'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Rutuja, though I think it depends on the dataset. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for signal processing? A cleaner experiment might isolate signal processing and keep everything else fixed.', 'a00061df-7c3e-4aa2-aab4-65a4b892e87e'::uuid, '2026-06-01T18:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7f6b7b26-44b7-4e4d-a928-3293f478b29e'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on signal processing. In our group we used signal processing on a small signal processing dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent. If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group. Keen to see follow-up results.', NULL::uuid, '2026-05-29T14:17:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('46c18009-705e-46cb-ac18-e67a4c83fe28'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the signal processing piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. The recent papers in our library on embedded systems would make a good companion read. In our group we used signal processing on a small signal processing dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-02T21:42:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('70456d64-03cf-4dcf-82b9-e3cf8d1f02a5'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Rutuja: the evidence for signal processing is thinner than it looks.', 'a00061df-7c3e-4aa2-aab4-65a4b892e87e'::uuid, '2026-06-01T21:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7ca05522-395f-44aa-aa96-72fdb5912de9'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the signal processing question deserves more attention than it gets. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say VLSI design? There is a useful parallel with VLSI design, where the role of signal processing is comparable. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-05-30T15:02:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('52aa51a8-af3f-489d-bb3a-17017ddd437e'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. One option is to run a small ablation on signal processing and share the numbers with the group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-03T14:14:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2313a986-689b-426e-b296-87bff11e5f0b'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. For context, the signal processing literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about data mining are to small changes in the data. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-17T00:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('29f41a35-826a-4f02-98a4-6136a113fa2e'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. For context, the sustainable finance literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. Last semester''s reading group went through “Proceedings of the Sixteenth ACM International Conference on Web…”, and most of the debate centred on web search.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-14T01:58:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0ac8ea3b-e108-4aaf-b2be-12bcea5d496f'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of the paper is less the headline number and more how it handles proceedings. There is a useful parallel with bioinformatics, where the role of web search is comparable. Our lab has been collecting notes on sixteenth ACM international conference; the picture is more nuanced than the abstract suggests. Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-16T08:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c19c5781-8eca-4737-aec9-335fa646c9bf'::uuid, 'Thanks Siddharth, that clarifies the web search part for me. Liability and transparency around data mining are still unsettled, and this paper does not address them. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', '29f41a35-826a-4f02-98a4-6136a113fa2e'::uuid, '2026-07-14T14:04:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c69b437b-2e59-4c20-b562-7419213b45ba'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around web search is easy to underestimate. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for data mining.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-19T03:07:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('12b77332-1cff-482c-9e6a-221efb672caf'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Proceedings of the Sixteenth ACM International Conference on Web…” is a useful lens on data mining. Is there a public dataset we could use to test proceedings ourselves?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-17T03:24:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('6f0362b0-c43f-4e9f-910b-12a074a74073'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around data mining easier to trust. For context, the sustainable finance literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-16T15:52:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c380e437-9501-4c3c-9677-bcdb6a6586c0'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on data mining for a while, so I''m glad it came up. Last semester''s reading group went through the paper, and most of the debate centred on web search. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-19T15:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fd13fbf2-4e7f-4742-ab21-ed993f347089'::uuid, 'Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the proceedings results?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-22T12:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7a490825-b963-42bc-a4e1-3cd7a9e46b33'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the intellectual capital piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around supply chain analytics easier to trust. A colleague''s project on supply chain analytics hit the same issue with artificial intelligence-based supply chain.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-22T13:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0acb05ee-1b42-49be-a41d-d56fc2448175'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “How artificial intelligence-based supply chain analytics enable supply chain…” is a useful lens on supply chain analytics. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from fintech adoption; the overlap with innovation looks real. It would help to see how intellectual capital performs for smaller organisations with limited data.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-25T01:17:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e93632fe-f2e9-4035-9c87-173f3f53145f'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. From a management perspective, the interesting part is the cost-benefit: what would adopting data privacy law change for a firm''s decisions?', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-19T11:09:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0af4d428-c0ab-454c-9d9b-7d6acf2a5b75'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Fatima: the evidence for balancing security is thinner than it looks. A colleague''s project on data privacy law hit the same issue with big data.', 'e93632fe-f2e9-4035-9c87-173f3f53145f'::uuid, '2026-11-21T17:27:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8c63278d-0d94-45f0-8b1e-d4e0bb99519a'::uuid, 'Agreed with Fatima on the main point. Related reading: surveys on bioinformatics cover the background on big data nicely. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one?', 'e93632fe-f2e9-4035-9c87-173f3f53145f'::uuid, '2026-11-22T09:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b80075f6-5ae5-45c2-a017-901d49b4e07a'::uuid, 'Thanks Vikram, that clarifies the balancing security part for me.', '0af4d428-c0ab-454c-9d9b-7d6acf2a5b75'::uuid, '2026-11-23T12:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9e791548-4240-4feb-88f8-9123ab623f8c'::uuid, 'Agreed with Vikram on the main point. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for data privacy law.', '0af4d428-c0ab-454c-9d9b-7d6acf2a5b75'::uuid, '2026-11-23T15:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9785f89f-3b40-4255-be13-c5a21d420e58'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the wireless sensor networks results?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-07T16:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('cbef39fe-6bc8-4cac-b8a8-d4b3ca6d3bdd'::uuid, 'Building on Rekha''s comment, the wireless sensor networks assumption matters a lot here. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs. Is there a public dataset we could use to test wireless sensor networks ourselves? Looking forward to hearing what others think.', '9785f89f-3b40-4255-be13-c5a21d420e58'::uuid, '2026-07-10T12:07:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0b0626e0-6335-4e1f-abb1-726ecef9c93a'::uuid, 'A cleaner experiment might isolate wireless sensor networks and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-30T12:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('623b087e-c1b3-4754-a5c0-d96b13cb5030'::uuid, 'Good point, Rekha; I had not considered that angle on wireless sensor networks. Consider tracking wireless sensor networks separately so that regressions are easier to spot. The social context of wireless sensor networks is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings.', '9785f89f-3b40-4255-be13-c5a21d420e58'::uuid, '2026-07-09T15:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('70e9061a-aa56-4b37-a8e7-3ee9849da1e0'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. A leaderboard number alone will not tell us whether work on wireless sensor networks is robust enough for deployment.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-04T21:14:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('897ee4f4-448e-4458-b3ec-5a0e81078453'::uuid, 'Rekha, that matches my experience too. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of wireless sensor networks. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for wireless sensor networks?', '9785f89f-3b40-4255-be13-c5a21d420e58'::uuid, '2026-07-07T19:16:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bce5c740-99c0-44e5-812b-89ead7e54e45'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a biosciences point of view. The recent papers in our library on VLSI design would make a good companion read. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding innovation. Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-08T16:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fb2302d1-7f5a-426a-bcb6-fda1c7378989'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on artificial intelligence regulation. The recent papers in our library on VLSI design would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-15T15:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5a2b408a-391e-42d6-a46b-bfce9b850996'::uuid, 'Gaurav, could you say more about how you handled innovation?', 'fb2302d1-7f5a-426a-bcb6-fda1c7378989'::uuid, '2026-06-15T17:15:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0b086a1e-af0f-4c27-88f5-fb4a979747dd'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split. Related reading: surveys on VLSI design cover the background on weighing ethical principles nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-14T12:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b09cabc7-3ab5-444c-a62b-5083ce2d50fe'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. This connects to the work on VLSI design, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. Is there a public dataset we could use to test weighing ethical principles ourselves?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-10T17:00:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bc7208b7-1d2a-4126-864f-79dbf56eb000'::uuid, 'Thanks Sneha, that clarifies the weighing ethical principles part for me. For context, the supply chain analytics literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. On our side the weighing ethical principles step was the bottleneck, not the main method. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', '0b086a1e-af0f-4c27-88f5-fb4a979747dd'::uuid, '2026-06-16T21:07:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz)
