  ('dee7f212-8819-4b1a-881f-6588e3722208'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the upheaval question deserves more attention than it gets. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one? The recent papers in our library on embedded systems would make a good companion read. Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-09T06:49:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0dcb3728-1433-43f8-8f0d-ad453b1ef44b'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Ishita, though I think it depends on the dataset. When we tried a similar setup for artificial intelligence regulation, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from upheaval versus simply more tuning. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', '2b5930a4-69ad-44c5-9f9d-8bd49c5151f7'::uuid, '2026-10-05T18:20:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('783a30e1-85fb-4580-881a-be41751e9c46'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Inaction on Artificial Intelligence Regulation in a Time of…” is a useful lens on artificial intelligence regulation. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of inaction.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-04T05:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b29e4600-4e2d-4ac4-adfe-aa184a5f75c1'::uuid, 'Sneha, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. It would help to state the assumptions behind upheaval formally and check which of them actually hold.', '783a30e1-85fb-4580-881a-be41751e9c46'::uuid, '2026-10-06T06:11:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9fe52ba5-2332-4971-ab97-ee92f70002d7'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. A cleaner experiment might isolate inaction and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-03T17:08:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('63592d3a-7600-4fb0-b216-8ee06fb01655'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. From a management perspective, the interesting part is the cost-benefit: what would adopting artificial intelligence regulation change for a firm''s decisions?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-09T05:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e52d52ef-15de-4666-98c0-666c166c3241'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on artificial intelligence regulation. The social context of artificial intelligence regulation is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-08T14:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0df05c70-df24-483a-b3e4-3dc88b4c90cc'::uuid, 'I skimmed “Determinants of Islamic fintech adoption” last week, and the framing of literature is the part I would discuss first. There is a useful parallel with computer vision, where the role of islamic fintech adoption is comparable. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-19T19:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ce9e9143-1226-4ae6-985c-f93498659a07'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on fintech adoption. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about fintech adoption are to small changes in the data. Consider tracking determinants separately so that regressions are easier to spot. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-13T19:46:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz)
