UPDATE comments c SET body = v.body, parent_comment_id = v.parent, created_at = v.ts FROM (VALUES
  ('8380f4d7-a246-4568-87ab-09300cf2f545'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of the paper is less the headline number and more how it handles literature. I would flag the privacy and public-policy implications of determinants before anyone builds on it. Consider tracking islamic fintech adoption separately so that regressions are easier to spot.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-14T22:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ac00820c-27ca-41c7-9196-03540b426403'::uuid, 'Mallika, that is a fair concern, and I will check it before drawing conclusions about fintech adoption. Did you check how it performs when the input around literature is noisy or partially missing? We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', '0df05c70-df24-483a-b3e4-3dc88b4c90cc'::uuid, '2026-10-21T11:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('271a84af-8267-48ae-a3ac-a6c5dd7fe12c'::uuid, 'Mallika, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper. There is a useful parallel with data mining, where the role of literature is comparable.', '0df05c70-df24-483a-b3e4-3dc88b4c90cc'::uuid, '2026-10-21T06:33:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0e117933-e0b8-4f55-84c0-56dc2a8e975f'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around digital divide is easy to underestimate. There is a regulatory angle here: work on fintech adoption raises questions about data governance, consent and accountability that we should map early. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around fintech adoption easier to trust. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-03T14:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e2694988-4104-4447-993d-692af5590edc'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. A colleague''s project on fintech adoption hit the same issue with determinants. The social context of fintech adoption is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-02T15:34:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e7a7aa01-7f35-4455-9cde-0350b52bdb48'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Bridging the Digital Divide” is less the headline number and more how it handles determinants. The social context of fintech adoption is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of bridging.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-08T11:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e5dbbe48-30d5-4f47-947f-31a69c030af4'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on fintech adoption.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-01T03:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0e3321a9-90d5-4d11-9b6c-54983a433d2d'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a biosciences point of view. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics. When we tried a similar setup for intellectual property, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-15T13:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('127e899e-a9f4-4d60-a109-96fe3e288e2e'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Tarun, though I think it depends on the dataset. Last semester''s reading group went through “Intellectual Property and Private International Law”, and most of the debate centred on private international law. For context, the synthetic biology literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', '0e3321a9-90d5-4d11-9b6c-54983a433d2d'::uuid, '2026-11-15T20:33:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('12a7b7db-4120-4a1e-917e-6390f04598f5'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the private international law question deserves more attention than it gets. Related reading: surveys on public policy cover the background on private international law nicely. I would add a humanities lens: how research on intellectual property is framed and interpreted matters as much as the technical result.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-20T14:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b2bc4bbd-bd31-4d85-838f-219f80b8a255'::uuid, 'I skimmed “Intellectual Property and Private International Law” last week, and the framing of private international law is the part I would discuss first. Related reading: surveys on supply chain analytics cover the background on private international law nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-14T17:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c599004b-c331-41dd-8ce3-53d5c708c137'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the public policies question deserves more attention than it gets. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about public policy in the wild.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-19T04:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0e460787-8a78-4593-97de-b111806a5aab'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. How does this compare with last year''s work on CRISPR gene editing? On our side the public policies step was the bottleneck, not the main method. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-19T14:54:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('342adfe0-5c41-47f0-8767-6b7dbf3223a9'::uuid, 'Helpful context, Manish. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of public policies.', 'c599004b-c331-41dd-8ce3-53d5c708c137'::uuid, '2026-10-19T22:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4e5847f4-11e8-4048-82d1-a529b6d576a5'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying protein folding in practice. On our side the disease step was the bottleneck, not the main method.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-11T09:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3f152854-28f3-45d6-ad0f-f72477b7a10f'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying protein folding in practice. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about protein folding in the wild. Related reading: surveys on fintech adoption cover the background on disease nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-10T22:07:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9ed6a8e0-7ceb-49c2-9a36-ad47ee3bf3b3'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Arjun: the evidence for disease is thinner than it looks. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around protein folding easier to trust. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one?', '3f152854-28f3-45d6-ad0f-f72477b7a10f'::uuid, '2026-11-13T15:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bfe62b7f-bff9-4f9a-b424-e692e8b15459'::uuid, 'Good point, Arjun; I had not considered that angle on protein folding.', '3f152854-28f3-45d6-ad0f-f72477b7a10f'::uuid, '2026-11-11T17:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0e5ac835-569c-49a7-b0d1-3119440e3247'::uuid, 'Building on Arjun''s comment, the tricky business assumption matters a lot here. A cleaner experiment might isolate disease and keep everything else fixed. For context, the supply chain analytics literature has been debating a very similar question for some time.', '3f152854-28f3-45d6-ad0f-f72477b7a10f'::uuid, '2026-11-11T04:26:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('65172099-4d8e-49a2-8a17-373e1d33750a'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Karthik, though I think it depends on the dataset. From a legal standpoint, how disease is documented will matter if the results are ever challenged. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for protein folding.', '0e5ac835-569c-49a7-b0d1-3119440e3247'::uuid, '2026-11-13T12:17:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4a37accb-5d21-4b64-9ea9-1a537a2adcb6'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Attention mechanisms in computer vision” is less the headline number and more how it handles attention mechanisms. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper. From a statistical point of view, I would want to see uncertainty estimates around the computer vision results, not only point values.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-15T03:23:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a89e4b46-1635-47af-9a74-0783eeaa589e'::uuid, 'Consider tracking attention mechanisms separately so that regressions are easier to spot.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-19T07:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7693560f-6347-438c-949e-e303c13acfda'::uuid, 'Good point, Shreya; I had not considered that angle on computer vision. Did you check how it performs when the input around attention mechanisms is noisy or partially missing? I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about computer vision in the wild.', 'a89e4b46-1635-47af-9a74-0783eeaa589e'::uuid, '2026-06-19T21:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0e70c898-01ac-4b36-8bba-ea7dd3ffb77b'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Adoption is usually limited by process and incentives, so any plan to adopt computer vision needs a realistic rollout story. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-18T17:20:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b3e24cd2-5333-4b29-abaf-2f572a58700c'::uuid, 'Ananya, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. There is a useful parallel with public policy, where the role of attention mechanisms is comparable. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around computer vision easier to trust.', '7693560f-6347-438c-949e-e303c13acfda'::uuid, '2026-06-20T10:39:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0ee2d1e0-3fe1-4607-9fa3-81f6a401d6d5'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying data privacy law in practice. We reproduced part of this for data privacy law and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-21T17:16:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
