  ('ea52f600-d6c8-40fb-9b27-01089bf347d3'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Intellectual Property” is a useful lens on intellectual property. On our side the intellectual property step was the bottleneck, not the main method. How does this compare with last year''s work on supply chain analytics?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-13T00:33:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4d8dbd24-1c9f-48dc-a191-edba045e561f'::uuid, 'Agreed with Tanvi on the main point. This connects to the work on supply chain analytics, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. Is there a public dataset we could use to test intellectual property ourselves? Looking forward to hearing what others think.', 'ea52f600-d6c8-40fb-9b27-01089bf347d3'::uuid, '2026-06-14T16:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('76bb601c-0ad4-4eed-8f33-4a24fc47eb86'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Intellectual Property” is less the headline number and more how it handles intellectual property. The recent papers in our library on supply chain analytics would make a good companion read. Did you check how it performs when the input around intellectual property is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-10T20:54:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0efc929f-7c93-4eb7-86c5-96afb7adb2b4'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Intellectual Property” is a useful lens on intellectual property. Did you check how it performs when the input around intellectual property is noisy or partially missing? It would be worth asking whose perspective is missing from the data behind intellectual property.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-19T06:02:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4b14d71f-e509-4098-8135-a0e6beb37bcd'::uuid, 'Tarun, could you say more about how you handled intellectual property? Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the intellectual property results? On our side the intellectual property step was the bottleneck, not the main method.', '4d8dbd24-1c9f-48dc-a191-edba045e561f'::uuid, '2026-06-14T19:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e850bf55-e7e1-4454-8398-2f6653a8c4b4'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Intellectual Property” is less the headline number and more how it handles intellectual property. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the intellectual property results hold. From a management perspective, the interesting part is the cost-benefit: what would adopting intellectual property change for a firm''s decisions?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-07T20:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('344b6e5b-d19b-4691-ac4c-4644d3825f26'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. Consider tracking regulatory drivers separately so that regressions are easier to spot.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-09T10:27:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('34f22493-2b94-4cf0-b542-be7ea65ad988'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Pallavi, though I think it depends on the dataset. It would help to state the assumptions behind data privacy laws formally and check which of them actually hold. On our side the regulatory drivers step was the bottleneck, not the main method. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', '344b6e5b-d19b-4691-ac4c-4644d3825f26'::uuid, '2026-11-11T14:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0f203442-f95a-4e17-81cb-eba8bc3e489b'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on data privacy law. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from graph neural networks; the overlap with regulatory drivers looks real. This connects to the work on graph neural networks, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-19T17:07:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0f3aecdf-8db6-4690-a33d-2d7014e001a8'::uuid, 'Consider tracking evaluation separately so that regressions are easier to spot.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-16T08:24:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4cdc5929-8b8a-48f1-985f-e2ca633472fb'::uuid, 'Helpful context, Rutuja. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one?', '0f3aecdf-8db6-4690-a33d-2d7014e001a8'::uuid, '2026-07-18T18:52:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f98a4932-66df-4a48-b6c3-ae9727c13079'::uuid, 'That is a fair summary, Rutuja, but one detail about large language models is missing. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from evaluation versus simply more tuning.', '0f3aecdf-8db6-4690-a33d-2d7014e001a8'::uuid, '2026-07-19T00:46:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8863c49e-d810-498b-9664-cf9f6da7af55'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying large language models in practice. In our group we used evaluation on a small large language models dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-20T13:54:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f0b14318-d098-4889-a482-02437efcf605'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the wireless sensor networks question deserves more attention than it gets. The social context of wireless sensor networks is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-03T22:34:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e1ee5401-8f00-484b-a914-dbd798732df0'::uuid, 'Radhika, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. When we tried a similar setup for wireless sensor networks, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', 'f0b14318-d098-4889-a482-02437efcf605'::uuid, '2026-06-05T20:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('0f3ec598-7c10-4e7d-b403-af1daf84d36c'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a engineering point of view. One option is to run a small ablation on wireless sensor networks and share the numbers with the group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-04T19:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c844939f-9119-4539-aca6-91dd7d928687'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Shreya: the evidence for wireless sensor networks is thinner than it looks. Computationally, the question is whether investing in wireless sensor networks still pays off once you account for training and inference cost.', 'e1ee5401-8f00-484b-a914-dbd798732df0'::uuid, '2026-06-06T21:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4b0a682e-f5fe-4ed7-a85a-730bb26b7430'::uuid, 'Good question. I read the paper a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. How does this compare with last year''s work on digital humanities?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-05T01:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5bb972a2-61c0-4b3b-af91-50708aa1d1d8'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Wireless Sensor Networks” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of wireless sensor networks.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-09T07:49:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
