  ('c6d13fcc-8105-4aac-81bb-e79416ee705c'::uuid, 'Priya, could you say more about how you handled computer vision approaches? I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about computer vision in the wild.', '13a84edc-5cd9-4057-94f4-469b70a530b5'::uuid, '2026-06-14T00:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dc037b89-6fa0-4dc2-8ee9-4a96ace6809f'::uuid, 'Good point, Pooja; I had not considered that angle on computer vision. In our group we used computer vision approaches on a small computer vision dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent.', 'bd304b2c-bb27-4fa6-9d57-4d0931d392b6'::uuid, '2026-06-13T01:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9f90e9e1-7e39-4257-a743-a5acc3c0f859'::uuid, 'I skimmed the paper last week, and the framing of synthetic image data is the part I would discuss first. How does this compare with last year''s work on public policy? Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-24T02:50:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f7956370-d414-44bc-9394-bf49909b0385'::uuid, 'Gaurav, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for computer vision? A colleague''s project on computer vision hit the same issue with synthetic image data.', '9f90e9e1-7e39-4257-a743-a5acc3c0f859'::uuid, '2026-08-26T14:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('472b3b89-ff37-46e9-bb2f-ca454d94f203'::uuid, 'Dev, could you say more about how you handled synthetic image data?', 'f7956370-d414-44bc-9394-bf49909b0385'::uuid, '2026-08-28T06:49:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c2c64ed5-ffe2-4056-be30-21571a9bbfb7'::uuid, 'Thanks Dev, this is exactly the feedback I was hoping for. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say digital humanities? We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', 'f7956370-d414-44bc-9394-bf49909b0385'::uuid, '2026-08-29T04:22:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('13b26774-0bba-48cc-9f90-05cd5331d15e'::uuid, 'Good point, Gaurav; I had not considered that angle on computer vision. It would help to state the assumptions behind synthetic image data formally and check which of them actually hold. Related reading: surveys on data mining cover the background on synthetic image data nicely.', '9f90e9e1-7e39-4257-a743-a5acc3c0f859'::uuid, '2026-08-26T09:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('13ffe917-31b6-4d8c-b7d1-849b6b65ddd8'::uuid, 'Quick follow-up to my post: I''ll keep a running list of what we learn about efficient heterogeneous graph neural here. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the efficient heterogeneous graph neural results? I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about graph neural networks in the wild. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-08T05:01:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('6eb716eb-cd4c-4c65-ab2b-f24bda2cb5dc'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the graph neural networks results hold. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-09T09:39:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ff10f455-9c84-4c25-ac03-a2fe6eee9ac7'::uuid, 'Suresh, that matches my experience too. I would like to see a measured latency figure rather than an estimate for graph neural networks.', '6eb716eb-cd4c-4c65-ab2b-f24bda2cb5dc'::uuid, '2026-11-10T19:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('975d5810-6ac6-4e60-8d64-dae95a682f99'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of embedded systems keeps coming up in our seminars. Our lab has been collecting notes on implementation; the picture is more nuanced than the abstract suggests.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-27T10:26:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('141d1b89-8182-49fa-8f21-009defa7bd49'::uuid, 'Good point, Varun; I had not considered that angle on embedded systems. For context, the fintech adoption literature has been debating a very similar question for some time.', '975d5810-6ac6-4e60-8d64-dae95a682f99'::uuid, '2026-09-30T06:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ce0cf0f5-ace1-41bd-b950-338e6f67542d'::uuid, 'Did you check how it performs when the input around embedded system is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-21T04:08:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f910f546-0777-4b1d-abc8-cfc262e4a0e1'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say digital humanities?', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-09T03:58:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('141daeb0-1d95-4074-b752-6abbd3e1b395'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying public policy in practice. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from literature versus simply more tuning. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about public policy are to small changes in the data. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-10T02:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8692beab-56f2-42b8-9e2e-53e08ad7d49c'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. A colleague''s project on public policy hit the same issue with literature. From a legal standpoint, how circular economy public policies is documented will matter if the results are ever challenged.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-19T14:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8b2cedbe-2ac9-422d-81e4-b50ba61faf93'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on public policy for a while, so I''m glad it came up. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-10T06:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f1adafd8-71f4-46d0-99cc-55185e70eb52'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. The social context of public policy is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings. In our group we used circular economy public policies on a small public policy dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-14T07:24:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f77c2a60-b6e7-4b5d-a8e2-0f6e97acf398'::uuid, 'I skimmed the paper last week, and the framing of circular economy public policies is the part I would discuss first. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from circular economy public policies versus simply more tuning.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-08T18:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5a829f98-8768-4d94-8b16-878e8a310699'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the literature results? One option is to run a small ablation on circular economy public policies and share the numbers with the group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-09T19:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz)
