  ('2d7dd695-9ec0-4302-845d-c3ce56192213'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around intangible supply chain analytical is easy to underestimate. There is a useful parallel with synthetic biology, where the role of unlocking supply chain agility is comparable. Consider tracking development separately so that regressions are easier to spot. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-02T04:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('15c966ce-7a3b-4d2e-82de-cd8c87b5cb57'::uuid, 'Thanks Pooja, that clarifies the unlocking supply chain agility part for me. Our lab has been collecting notes on development; the picture is more nuanced than the abstract suggests. I would like to see a simple analytical baseline for supply chain performance through before trusting the more elaborate method.', '2d7dd695-9ec0-4302-845d-c3ce56192213'::uuid, '2026-07-03T15:49:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4c3e5698-249a-4d7b-9abd-131d0148ef4e'::uuid, 'That is a fair summary, Bhavana, but one detail about supply chain analytics is missing. This connects to the work on synthetic biology, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group.', '15c966ce-7a3b-4d2e-82de-cd8c87b5cb57'::uuid, '2026-07-04T01:27:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('cd0d9d36-903b-4602-a552-13dda416edd0'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for unlocking supply chain agility? When we tried a similar setup for supply chain analytics, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-07T03:23:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('56e43db9-a55a-43e4-88eb-f69c22431983'::uuid, 'Thanks Rekha, that clarifies the intangible supply chain analytical part for me. There is a useful parallel with graph neural networks, where the role of development is comparable. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for supply chain analytics.', 'cd0d9d36-903b-4602-a552-13dda416edd0'::uuid, '2026-07-08T01:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f7ba8caa-b0d3-425e-ac12-666540ecdd5f'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Unlocking supply chain agility and supply chain performance through…” is less the headline number and more how it handles development. When we tried a similar setup for supply chain analytics, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-29T10:49:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('40399e27-9731-4807-b2d4-f6fa7de22bd8'::uuid, 'Thanks Bhavana, that clarifies the development part for me. How does this compare with last year''s work on cyber law? From a legal standpoint, how supply chain performance through is documented will matter if the results are ever challenged.', '15c966ce-7a3b-4d2e-82de-cd8c87b5cb57'::uuid, '2026-07-03T16:58:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('15dc0d82-b7a5-401c-9d86-fb3cab4b83fb'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the magnetogenetics question deserves more attention than it gets. For context, the artificial intelligence regulation literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. How does this compare with last year''s work on artificial intelligence regulation?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-11T16:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fda08bdd-3471-46da-b32f-dfc330b8f814'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around magnetogenetics is easy to underestimate. I would add a humanities lens: how research on CRISPR gene editing is framed and interpreted matters as much as the technical result. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from magnetogenetics versus simply more tuning.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-13T16:34:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2d007546-22d1-425e-9a08-75ad1d7fc13e'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Public-facing claims about piezo mechanosensitive ion channel deserve careful wording, since non-specialists will read them very differently.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-18T22:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('322eb92f-01d7-4100-a262-47a0d32e6eff'::uuid, 'I skimmed the paper last week, and the framing of magnetogenetics is the part I would discuss first. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say synthetic biology?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-14T07:56:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('15feaa7d-7049-48c7-9653-c2a27e3c50c6'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Toward Requirements for Embedded Systems” is less the headline number and more how it handles requirements. I would like to see a simple analytical baseline for requirements before trusting the more elaborate method. Did you check how it performs when the input around requirements is noisy or partially missing? I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-13T07:46:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
