  ('187512c0-7e1a-4245-8453-16ba2b7bf29f'::uuid, 'Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one?', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-17T01:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('16b1b207-0feb-4328-8053-f6bdb9a02361'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the supply chain resilience piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from VLSI design; the overlap with triple-a supply chains looks real. Related reading: surveys on VLSI design cover the background on supply chain resilience nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-12T02:09:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('cb1cc779-fb0c-4318-b7af-abfa61e3f298'::uuid, 'Thanks Vikram, that clarifies the triple-a supply chains part for me. One option is to run a small ablation on supply chain resilience and share the numbers with the group. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one? Looking forward to hearing what others think.', '16b1b207-0feb-4328-8053-f6bdb9a02361'::uuid, '2026-08-14T08:00:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('53bf11cc-579d-48b2-91d3-4b1130298824'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Vikram: the evidence for triple-a supply chains is thinner than it looks.', '16b1b207-0feb-4328-8053-f6bdb9a02361'::uuid, '2026-08-12T17:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
