  ('857c3541-84b1-4048-8d92-6096bc4f081a'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. For context, the embedded systems literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say embedded systems?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-27T14:10:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4bf792ee-7e46-4196-8bcd-657cd08769db'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying signal processing in practice. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding graph signal processing.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-23T20:58:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('17026a2b-9715-4fd9-8cc1-1425f05db8ee'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the graph signal processing piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. How does this compare with last year''s work on embedded systems?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-24T12:27:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('838a7ead-aca8-4baa-9642-c5395c44df62'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on signal processing. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of graph signal processing. Is there a public dataset we could use to test graph signal processing ourselves? I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-31T19:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
