  ('1beb0555-4e68-40c1-a9f1-cd91df531b9a'::uuid, 'I skimmed “CREATIVE INDUSTRIES IN MEDIA STUDIES” last week, and the framing of MEDIA STUDIES is the part I would discuss first. A colleague''s project on media studies hit the same issue with CREATIVE INDUSTRIES. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-03T17:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dd11985f-bb26-4fed-bfe3-a3bfdd7fb6a8'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on protein folding. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around protein folding easier to trust. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for protein folding? Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-28T12:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('1bfb2f56-e6d0-458a-acb1-584b23fad324'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the folding variations question deserves more attention than it gets. Is there a public dataset we could use to test folding variations ourselves? Related reading: surveys on graph neural networks cover the background on folding variations nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-27T19:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('32b2c550-98d8-4c70-a6c3-1b8cf5e645f4'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a biosciences point of view. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from attention mechanisms versus simply more tuning. One option is to run a small ablation on attention mechanisms and share the numbers with the group. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-02T16:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('aec28b96-f6ba-4f66-9c5e-76e7a571f2f6'::uuid, 'Charulatha, could you say more about how you handled attention mechanisms?', '32b2c550-98d8-4c70-a6c3-1b8cf5e645f4'::uuid, '2026-08-05T00:41:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
