  ('402b5916-f6a1-466c-855c-f1daf30399ff'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Attention mechanisms in computer vision” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. The recent papers in our library on intellectual property would make a good companion read. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-26T16:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('1c756d5a-78cb-4a7d-b5b3-cf57d47ae9b8'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a mathematical point of view. It would help to state the assumptions behind attention mechanisms formally and check which of them actually hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-27T09:04:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ab90cb96-9ba9-4719-b27f-04a08c173b4b'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say data privacy law? I would flag the privacy and public-policy implications of multimodel large language models before anyone builds on it.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-03T19:14:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('1c94aa0a-c390-440b-ac66-ee6725a6a600'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around multimodel large language models is easy to underestimate. Related reading: surveys on artificial intelligence regulation cover the background on multimodel large language models nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-05T22:08:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
