  ('dd2d442b-1a7f-4254-95b5-2fd7977fc1ba'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Trevor Pinch’s legacy for media studies” is a useful lens on media studies. Last semester''s reading group went through “Trevor Pinch’s legacy for media studies”, and most of the debate centred on trevor pinch s legacy. The recent papers in our library on large language models would make a good companion read. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-11T11:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c595c136-9c4f-4226-a913-f4ef5d9ce197'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. The social context of media studies is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-11T12:22:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('79803c9a-ed9f-4273-9f97-cac262b88a8e'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Rohan. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about media studies in the wild. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for media studies? Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', 'dd2d442b-1a7f-4254-95b5-2fd7977fc1ba'::uuid, '2026-07-11T22:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
