  ('24d205b8-dd18-4075-8a8b-558acfe5d12d'::uuid, 'I skimmed “Evaluation of CRISPR gene-editing tools in zebrafish” last week, and the framing of CRISPR gene-editing tools is the part I would discuss first. When we tried a similar setup for CRISPR gene editing, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did. A cleaner experiment might isolate evaluation and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-20T05:02:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('204313a2-4691-4739-9aa5-41ceac798b6c'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Evaluation of CRISPR gene-editing tools in zebrafish” is a useful lens on CRISPR gene editing. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about CRISPR gene editing are to small changes in the data. Is there a public dataset we could use to test zebrafish ourselves?', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-15T04:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4d3d21cf-5cd1-4851-8d94-92ea4f3ed8e6'::uuid, 'Aditi, that is a fair concern, and I will check it before drawing conclusions about CRISPR gene editing. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding zebrafish.', '204313a2-4691-4739-9aa5-41ceac798b6c'::uuid, '2026-11-15T15:13:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3dcccafe-05a1-4846-89e3-5a79c04a5e79'::uuid, 'Thanks Aditi, that clarifies the zebrafish part for me. Adoption is usually limited by process and incentives, so any plan to adopt CRISPR gene editing needs a realistic rollout story.', '204313a2-4691-4739-9aa5-41ceac798b6c'::uuid, '2026-11-17T14:52:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
