  ('23be3aeb-db87-4567-9fd7-80b6c829a0eb'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a mathematical point of view. The recent papers in our library on public policy would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-11T13:48:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('da6ee8f4-7797-430b-a61c-a71934b15b3b'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around modified signal routing algorithm is easy to underestimate. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics. I would flag the privacy and public-policy implications of modified signal routing algorithm before anyone builds on it. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-06T10:56:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('79aa37e7-adef-4a73-80ad-1d30beb3b68f'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the intellectual property question deserves more attention than it gets. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for artificial intelligence? Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-08T02:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('23d90ab4-c033-4b0a-8f5c-b84a579a1ec1'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the complexities piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. For context, the cognitive psychology literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for artificial intelligence? Keen to see follow-up results.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-06T09:48:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('df248864-7c79-41af-a961-1a243afb01c2'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Is Protein Folding a Thermodynamically Unfavorable, Active, Energy-Dependent Process?” is less the headline number and more how it handles energy-dependent process. There is a useful parallel with synthetic biology, where the role of thermodynamically unfavorable is comparable. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-18T04:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d2c97619-e628-42ff-b8ff-c4518287bab6'::uuid, 'Good point, Rohan; I had not considered that angle on protein folding. We reproduced part of this for protein folding and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower.', 'df248864-7c79-41af-a961-1a243afb01c2'::uuid, '2026-06-20T18:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('cfe40235-d16a-4d7b-9c87-bded6151e1b0'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying protein folding in practice. One option is to run a small ablation on energy-dependent process and share the numbers with the group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-25T23:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fe723e60-7b81-40f2-a7a0-202c83f8ca30'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Rohan: the evidence for energy-dependent process is thinner than it looks. Is there a public dataset we could use to test thermodynamically unfavorable ourselves? It could be worth pairing this with ideas from digital humanities; the overlap with energy-dependent process looks real.', 'df248864-7c79-41af-a961-1a243afb01c2'::uuid, '2026-06-19T12:13:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('23dbfd65-e0fa-44df-9f53-8fcf5d51991b'::uuid, 'Rohan, that matches my experience too.', 'df248864-7c79-41af-a961-1a243afb01c2'::uuid, '2026-06-20T07:11:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('240bbf9e-9a08-43a5-a322-d4b6a9c8ef16'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying digital humanities in practice. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input. The recent papers in our library on synthetic biology would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-06T18:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4d71cbcd-3b69-4289-bb37-6a42ffe4a8fc'::uuid, 'Good question. I read the paper a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. Related reading: surveys on protein folding cover the background on librarianship nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-09T03:42:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('671edf90-203c-4542-8d54-5405e4597ab5'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Computer Vision” is a useful lens on computer vision. It would help to see how computer vision performs for smaller organisations with limited data. If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-21T17:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d7c7a10e-3340-45c6-b656-c692305cc5f2'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the computer vision question deserves more attention than it gets. The recent papers in our library on signal processing would make a good companion read. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about computer vision in the wild.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-19T20:56:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bdba7327-7b2c-4d48-a376-5937a45ab2c0'::uuid, 'Thanks Abhishek, that clarifies the computer vision part for me.', 'd7c7a10e-3340-45c6-b656-c692305cc5f2'::uuid, '2026-10-22T14:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2411195c-bd59-4134-8307-e8e43346499e'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Ananya. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for computer vision.', 'bdba7327-7b2c-4d48-a376-5937a45ab2c0'::uuid, '2026-10-23T08:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5f04c352-5d20-400b-bf51-3041d43c3e8d'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on wireless sensor networks for a while, so I''m glad it came up. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about wireless sensor networks are to small changes in the data.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-03T23:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d02b2c7c-e890-4116-a75a-8bc2e26ed4d6'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on wireless sensor networks. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the wireless sensor networks results hold. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs. Keen to see follow-up results.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-31T21:26:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a7953a00-75a0-4fc5-a558-6b347b4eea97'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Wireless Sensor Networks for Precision Agriculture” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about wireless sensor networks are to small changes in the data.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-09T23:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7f371214-7b46-4dc1-a9b6-978eb5ed7678'::uuid, 'Agreed with Rahul on the main point. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? Related reading: surveys on bioinformatics cover the background on NPK sensor implementations nicely.', '5f04c352-5d20-400b-bf51-3041d43c3e8d'::uuid, '2026-09-04T14:07:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
