  ('4d95121b-218d-45ae-b0d8-719724a52d09'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from GENETIC CODE versus simply more tuning.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-19T06:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('249553be-06b0-4876-8b62-850995b1f235'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “GENETIC CODE OF PROTEIN FOLDING” is a useful lens on protein folding. Our lab has been collecting notes on PROTEIN FOLDING; the picture is more nuanced than the abstract suggests. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-16T07:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8d57d87f-3eca-4f1d-917e-541ddfc52df9'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a biosciences point of view. A colleague''s project on protein folding hit the same issue with GENETIC CODE. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around protein folding easier to trust. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-12T11:27:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('cfc35de9-04e5-453f-94dc-4acd2a2771c3'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a biosciences point of view. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? We reproduced part of this for artificial intelligence regulation and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-16T07:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('24bb58c3-015c-477c-8b84-7dd3a65764a2'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a biosciences point of view. There is a useful parallel with CRISPR gene editing, where the role of ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE REGULATION is comparable. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-12T20:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2ad84848-cf88-4b41-80a9-62954039c1a9'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE REGULATION is easy to underestimate. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of EUROPEAN UNION s APPROACH.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-07T07:09:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('27eac9ab-abaa-4836-a084-e5b5d604030a'::uuid, 'I skimmed “THE EUROPEAN UNION’S APPROACH TO ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE REGULATION” last week, and the framing of ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE REGULATION is the part I would discuss first. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about artificial intelligence regulation in the wild. One option is to run a small ablation on ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE REGULATION and share the numbers with the group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-16T11:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ec4e9c5d-8d01-4997-b8d0-5eef07163955'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the large language models piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. Last semester''s reading group went through “A Comprehensive Overview of Large Language Models”, and most of the debate centred on large language models. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-02T09:50:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz)
