  ('2a394ad4-b48a-472a-b621-ad35d9f3949d'::uuid, 'Rahul, could you say more about how you handled cognitive psychology? How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around cognitive psychology easier to trust. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', 'f5b879d7-ed47-407a-a6d2-4a6e7a24f1ba'::uuid, '2026-05-28T13:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7376a0a3-1c7b-4a06-ae19-c32e3b0c60ab'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. Consider tracking cognitive psychology separately so that regressions are easier to spot. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say data mining?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-04T03:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bf231acb-7d1d-4181-8d8d-c61a510235ea'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. This connects to the work on sustainable finance, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. How does this compare with last year''s work on sustainable finance? Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-20T03:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8124bf82-a5c4-410b-b977-05e14f12291e'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the medical field question deserves more attention than it gets. The recent papers in our library on consumer behavior would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-22T09:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e92acd1c-2dc1-4e20-aa42-de078ce1c0f4'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of the paper is less the headline number and more how it handles medical field. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding medical field.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-23T18:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2a412f63-f274-4880-9dad-b544eb767b5b'::uuid, 'Agreed with Mallika on the main point. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', 'e92acd1c-2dc1-4e20-aa42-de078ce1c0f4'::uuid, '2026-11-24T06:40:11.587261+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9c14abb9-1672-4a18-a0ae-f7b113dd740d'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on embedded systems for a while, so I''m glad it came up. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about embedded systems are to small changes in the data.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-15T00:23:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e40e950a-4337-4c9e-ace3-1d13825add96'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a humanities and social sciences point of view. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of qualitative research methods. When we tried a similar setup for media studies, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-21T16:02:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2a7ba9a3-b76b-4a94-9e81-4ff3e630a512'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of media studies keeps coming up in our seminars. The recent papers in our library on intellectual property would make a good companion read. Last semester''s reading group went through “Qualitative Research Methods for Media Studies”, and most of the debate centred on qualitative research methods. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-24T12:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('99d8849c-667c-4f92-aa68-1374a3f7a121'::uuid, 'Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for media studies?', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-25T04:36:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c9531a28-53ec-4502-8fd5-cdd31255bed7'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the qualitative research methods question deserves more attention than it gets. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about media studies are to small changes in the data.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-20T20:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d852407a-b011-477f-b91a-11cb0f8bd8aa'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around qualitative research methods is easy to underestimate. I would flag the privacy and public-policy implications of qualitative research methods before anyone builds on it.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-20T23:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('82987559-1d48-4d2c-8965-e70fea1146b2'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the qualitative research methods piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from intellectual property; the overlap with qualitative research methods looks real.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-26T03:50:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b5b2f58a-00d9-4dc3-a974-a99f4b93b5d6'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Qualitative Research Methods for Media Studies” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. Did you check how it performs when the input around qualitative research methods is noisy or partially missing? It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from qualitative research methods versus simply more tuning.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-21T17:33:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f8f670c1-e687-436c-85f0-db6754bac301'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the changing world question deserves more attention than it gets. Adoption is usually limited by process and incentives, so any plan to adopt cognitive psychology needs a realistic rollout story. If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-30T06:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4b5b7067-1693-4dfd-89e5-75f9285c8d6f'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around changing world is easy to underestimate. Liability and transparency around cognitive psychology are still unsettled, and this paper does not address them. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the cognitive psychology results hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-31T17:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5136b4fd-5739-415a-9639-34ec8f2e2fc1'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Cognitive Psychology in a Changing World” is less the headline number and more how it handles changing world. Public-facing claims about changing world deserve careful wording, since non-specialists will read them very differently.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-31T02:49:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('2ab2ade1-9b86-4c9e-aa26-6274f416e1db'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on cognitive psychology for a while, so I''m glad it came up. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for changing world?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-28T02:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
