  ('3dc27f7d-0d78-4dea-b532-5a0d17edda3c'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the translation rates question deserves more attention than it gets. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? When we tried a similar setup for protein folding, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-13T08:11:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('90939ed9-04d1-4bc5-824e-0406144033d1'::uuid, 'Thanks Sneha, that clarifies the translation rates part for me. The recent papers in our library on supply chain analytics would make a good companion read.', '31fee17e-531b-4832-a986-d07376cc7616'::uuid, '2026-11-11T01:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a31efce5-8bca-46fc-a969-69b7bdea6c61'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a biosciences point of view. Is there a public dataset we could use to test translation rates ourselves? A cleaner experiment might isolate translation rates and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-14T19:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4d62c5b4-87db-467d-97fb-cfef8f320d70'::uuid, 'Good question. I read the paper a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. The social context of intellectual property is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings. A colleague''s project on intellectual property hit the same issue with ENTERPRISE DEVELOPMENT.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-17T09:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4cbb6155-8eb6-40bd-acd3-576a4749cd79'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Consider tracking ENTERPRISE DEVELOPMENT separately so that regressions are easier to spot.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-06T00:11:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('321f6b57-d45d-41a7-a2d8-0cc35604a697'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on intellectual property. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding STRATEGIC MANAGEMENT. I would like to see a simple analytical baseline for INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY before trusting the more elaborate method.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-15T05:10:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('92fa4b13-825f-4390-bf5e-ab7bf097ff03'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on CRISPR gene editing.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-27T00:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('32502c77-ea59-4742-af9f-9e7f438d274a'::uuid, 'Tarun, could you say more about how you handled CRISPR gene editing technology?', '92fa4b13-825f-4390-bf5e-ab7bf097ff03'::uuid, '2026-10-28T07:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('47bed360-bb12-4569-977d-c012503ff3a5'::uuid, 'Agreed with Tarun on the main point. From a statistical point of view, I would want to see uncertainty estimates around the CRISPR gene editing results, not only point values.', '92fa4b13-825f-4390-bf5e-ab7bf097ff03'::uuid, '2026-10-29T07:00:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('64824d67-ffb3-4f02-a076-1628ec8d42cf'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Tarun. Our lab has been collecting notes on CRISPR gene editing technology; the picture is more nuanced than the abstract suggests. Is there a public dataset we could use to test potential ourselves?', '92fa4b13-825f-4390-bf5e-ab7bf097ff03'::uuid, '2026-10-27T17:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('761a5dc2-5b8d-487a-aef1-9863d828220d'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around alphafold fails is easy to underestimate. Our lab has been collecting notes on predict protein fold switching; the picture is more nuanced than the abstract suggests.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-11T22:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('eca1b963-d6ad-40c6-ba69-32c5cf7abd8d'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a humanities and social sciences point of view. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for alphafold fails? Related reading: surveys on media studies cover the background on predict protein fold switching nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-10T16:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b638f865-ed88-4f1f-8a0b-34e0ded97f8c'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Siddharth, though I think it depends on the dataset. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? A negative control would make the protein folding claims much easier to interpret in a lab setting.', 'eca1b963-d6ad-40c6-ba69-32c5cf7abd8d'::uuid, '2026-11-11T03:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fdab2c80-9352-4e88-8ae8-6718ad834f3d'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “AlphaFold2 fails to predict protein fold switching” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. We reproduced part of this for protein folding and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower. This connects to the work on embedded systems, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-14T00:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('78208e36-8386-46f5-ba25-0d10c262711e'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the alphafold fails question deserves more attention than it gets. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the predict protein fold switching results? A cleaner experiment might isolate alphafold fails and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-08T05:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('33a25e67-86e3-448c-bc8e-e2b99ba154a4'::uuid, 'I skimmed the paper last week, and the framing of predict protein fold switching is the part I would discuss first. On our side the alphafold fails step was the bottleneck, not the main method. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-13T18:20:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c2ec7891-8f06-40cf-a650-a77c64773b71'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of protein folding keeps coming up in our seminars. A cleaner experiment might isolate alphafold fails and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-11T11:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3bd919d7-72b1-4dd5-b2e0-5d3f1e21d27a'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of consumer behavior keeps coming up in our seminars. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding marketing. This connects to the work on fintech adoption, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-27T18:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('77ca0767-4af9-4c6a-b22a-173e18a93493'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the marketing question deserves more attention than it gets. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around consumer behavior easier to trust.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-27T08:00:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('789e14f7-ccf9-4ab2-a86b-d4f0994dc0c8'::uuid, 'That is a fair summary, Omkar, but one detail about consumer behavior is missing. A colleague''s project on consumer behavior hit the same issue with marketing. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for consumer behavior? I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', '3bd919d7-72b1-4dd5-b2e0-5d3f1e21d27a'::uuid, '2026-06-27T19:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('33bdda33-7ee4-4880-8701-0350c6feacd8'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Consumer behavior and marketing” is a useful lens on consumer behavior. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about consumer behavior in the wild. How does this compare with last year''s work on embedded systems? Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-29T09:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('35bc9792-5f3c-41c3-8b3f-740bd9f7434d'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Synthetic Biology‐Based Engineering Cells for Drug Delivery” is a useful lens on synthetic biology. From a legal standpoint, how engineering cells is documented will matter if the results are ever challenged.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-12T09:33:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c1baa0bb-82f8-46c7-8e7b-d6d48a815026'::uuid, 'I skimmed “Synthetic Biology‐Based Engineering Cells for Drug Delivery” last week, and the framing of engineering cells is the part I would discuss first. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-05T06:34:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9457d6ba-6a41-4078-afb6-86d1fa0791d8'::uuid, 'That is a fair summary, Shreya, but one detail about synthetic biology is missing.', '35bc9792-5f3c-41c3-8b3f-740bd9f7434d'::uuid, '2026-09-12T10:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8630bc8a-94f4-485b-8711-a9529838873b'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. We reproduced part of this for synthetic biology and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-01T21:22:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('343ca7ac-c046-41a2-ae19-7c2e6d91e5e8'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Meera. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from engineering cells versus simply more tuning. On our side the drug delivery step was the bottleneck, not the main method.', 'c1baa0bb-82f8-46c7-8e7b-d6d48a815026'::uuid, '2026-09-06T14:37:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('346a3ffc-82a1-4614-ad60-2e20d36fbf10'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. A cleaner experiment might isolate signal processing and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-30T03:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dceaedf7-9b42-4ede-8bf8-19563d028e16'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of the paper is less the headline number and more how it handles signal processing. The recent papers in our library on CRISPR gene editing would make a good companion read. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for signal processing.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-21T17:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9fbb451f-962e-47df-acf8-aedc5e4197b1'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Priya: the evidence for signal processing is thinner than it looks. There is a useful parallel with embedded systems, where the role of signal processing is comparable.', 'dceaedf7-9b42-4ede-8bf8-19563d028e16'::uuid, '2026-07-22T22:20:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f7f6c1b2-26aa-4071-a6fb-197879e46f78'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around signal processing is easy to underestimate. The social context of signal processing is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings. Related reading: surveys on public policy cover the background on signal processing nicely. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-29T09:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c268e71c-7715-435b-bd89-c89f6bd10138'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. There is a regulatory angle here: work on signal processing raises questions about data governance, consent and accountability that we should map early. If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-19T17:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f7bcf77c-c36f-400d-9b88-b99af72331fd'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the optimization algorithms piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-19T19:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('67596217-a7ac-4249-9031-ed54f81a9752'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on wireless sensor networks for a while, so I''m glad it came up. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input. The recent papers in our library on bioinformatics would make a good companion read. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-14T17:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f5e688d3-66e6-44c2-a187-de676e0287d5'::uuid, 'Saving this; the wireless sensor networks node angle is useful.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-11T06:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c269db10-fe8d-4c6e-b77e-f81a2c08561d'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-16T18:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('48d3a012-d3ec-4197-8298-2e6c3fbecb7d'::uuid, 'Good catch, Tanvi. I should have been clearer about the setup around wireless sensor networks node. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from optimization algorithms versus simply more tuning.', 'f5e688d3-66e6-44c2-a187-de676e0287d5'::uuid, '2026-10-11T07:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('37ca38f9-ab71-4e63-82ae-bf9745a28d82'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the wireless sensor networks node piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for optimization algorithms?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-18T23:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('34744499-1b67-4d19-aa8e-6dbb2c57deb2'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a management point of view. Adoption is usually limited by process and incentives, so any plan to adopt wireless sensor networks needs a realistic rollout story.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-16T17:01:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7779ed4c-4ee3-4214-9071-622501c127cb'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying large language models in practice. A cleaner experiment might isolate large language models and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-26T02:10:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
