  ('34a3dbe4-f2b9-4103-afc0-71ded78c2b0f'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of large language models keeps coming up in our seminars. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-23T14:13:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fc810f92-aa74-489f-8871-c360ea7a8e58'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Aditya: the evidence for large language models is thinner than it looks. Consider tracking large language models separately so that regressions are easier to spot. On our side the large language models step was the bottleneck, not the main method.', '791dc496-d0af-48d3-bceb-6ef72235c9a0'::uuid, '2026-10-29T02:37:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dd1d5931-1db3-432f-b624-39e6db5fa31e'::uuid, 'Building on Aditya''s comment, the large language models assumption matters a lot here. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the large language models results hold.', '791dc496-d0af-48d3-bceb-6ef72235c9a0'::uuid, '2026-10-31T14:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('62be5a88-959f-46f6-ba87-3f44aa29d50f'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Embedded Systems” is less the headline number and more how it handles embedded systems. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input. It would help to see how embedded systems performs for smaller organisations with limited data. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-08T19:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('34e6e470-404e-4965-8d95-52a348a1b34d'::uuid, 'Helpful context, Karthik. Consider tracking embedded systems separately so that regressions are easier to spot. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', '62be5a88-959f-46f6-ba87-3f44aa29d50f'::uuid, '2026-08-11T07:28:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
