  ('7a95d4fa-c320-415b-8c42-9cf106f4647d'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of embedded systems keeps coming up in our seminars. The recent papers in our library on synthetic biology would make a good companion read. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around embedded systems easier to trust.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-02T21:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('350a6f6e-b79d-49b6-b166-52ee4543713c'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the challenges results? Adoption is usually limited by process and incentives, so any plan to adopt large language models needs a realistic rollout story.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-24T21:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ed0adb58-c318-464a-971d-7c29ff208898'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Challenges and Applications of Large Language Models” is a useful lens on large language models. The recent papers in our library on data mining would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-21T11:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3c8858c3-c1c5-42f1-8bc5-a6e3f292c6bd'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Fatima. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one? On our side the applications step was the bottleneck, not the main method.', '350a6f6e-b79d-49b6-b166-52ee4543713c'::uuid, '2026-10-25T03:26:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('895fba94-d2bf-4a65-aced-c5b82a1744b0'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the challenges piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. From a statistical point of view, I would want to see uncertainty estimates around the large language models results, not only point values. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from data mining; the overlap with challenges looks real. Keen to see follow-up results.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-24T11:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c3d01b1c-02e6-477e-b4ee-8357518fd6b6'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Challenges and Applications of Large Language Models” is a useful lens on large language models. Liability and transparency around large language models are still unsettled, and this paper does not address them. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper. Keen to see follow-up results.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-21T02:39:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7ecc668e-1efc-4981-af19-3b41f9cdcdf9'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Spatio-Temporal Graph Neural Networks” is less the headline number and more how it handles spatio-temporal graph neural networks. When we tried a similar setup for graph neural networks, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did. For context, the digital humanities literature has been debating a very similar question for some time.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-06T08:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fa0c1d5d-9d3a-4a8a-b333-a78878802099'::uuid, 'Swati, could you say more about how you handled spatio-temporal graph neural networks? Is there a public dataset we could use to test spatio-temporal graph neural networks ourselves? This connects to the work on supply chain analytics, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', '7ecc668e-1efc-4981-af19-3b41f9cdcdf9'::uuid, '2026-11-08T22:52:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
