  ('b56a5818-07ca-4ca2-9680-4b2327a6b0b4'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on cognitive psychology. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-27T02:41:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('384acca4-73ce-4615-96d0-9f3696d97409'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the applied cognitive psychology master piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. There is a useful parallel with protein folding, where the role of applied cognitive psychology master is comparable.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-22T10:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7fbca7f7-b243-4878-9cc8-6372c024ab1a'::uuid, 'That is a fair summary, Rutuja, but one detail about cognitive psychology is missing. The social context of cognitive psychology is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings.', '384acca4-73ce-4615-96d0-9f3696d97409'::uuid, '2026-10-23T13:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('42478387-3bbb-4f5f-88ce-d4670e80b139'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. How does this compare with last year''s work on consumer behavior? A colleague''s project on VLSI design hit the same issue with prediction.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-07T13:24:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('484e2440-a82d-4f0b-bd2e-50a163653075'::uuid, 'I see it a little differently, Mallika. For context, the digital humanities literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of anomaly detection.', '42478387-3bbb-4f5f-88ce-d4670e80b139'::uuid, '2026-10-09T01:37:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bfb3394b-bc5e-4e18-9293-a68ce871bf8b'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. For context, the protein folding literature has been debating a very similar question for some time.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-07T06:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('35bf90f0-5f1e-40dc-b6c7-c3a834825b0e'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around VLSI design workflows is easy to underestimate. In our group we used anomaly detection on a small VLSI design dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-15T15:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('35d8d0aa-177e-4a18-8c81-7eaa5a7f4fcd'::uuid, 'Quick follow-up to my post: I''ll keep a running list of what we learn about federated learning here. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split. Consider tracking federated learning separately so that regressions are easier to spot. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-27T20:22:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a70f7cd9-1907-4414-aab9-d7940abb291f'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on computer vision. Computationally, the question is whether investing in federated learning still pays off once you account for training and inference cost. On our side the federated learning step was the bottleneck, not the main method.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-20T18:15:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7e294a83-2453-4e38-a858-26a993642654'::uuid, 'I skimmed the paper last week, and the framing of federated learning is the part I would discuss first. It would be worth asking whose perspective is missing from the data behind federated learning.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-18T18:58:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5d9e43c8-4a09-46d5-b109-fa503749212c'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on computer vision for a while, so I''m glad it came up. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding federated learning. I would want evidence that federated learning translates into measurable business outcomes, not only better metrics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-21T10:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8775cce6-1148-4660-a97c-7f1512fcbf9b'::uuid, 'Mallika, that matches my experience too. On our side the federated learning step was the bottleneck, not the main method. It would help to state the assumptions behind federated learning formally and check which of them actually hold.', '5d9e43c8-4a09-46d5-b109-fa503749212c'::uuid, '2026-07-22T13:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('45bea74c-10ce-490d-81b2-1c27c8a6c343'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a management point of view. A cleaner experiment might isolate federated learning and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-30T14:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('35f8098f-d8b0-4721-bfce-70def1106d89'::uuid, 'I skimmed “Consumer behavior in the metaverse” last week, and the framing of metaverse is the part I would discuss first. A colleague''s project on consumer behavior hit the same issue with metaverse. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the metaverse results? Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-06T17:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d4f4eb70-6301-4ef1-97b5-53326af6b9d0'::uuid, 'Good point, Fatima; I had not considered that angle on consumer behavior. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics. It would be worth asking whose perspective is missing from the data behind metaverse. Keen to see follow-up results.', '35f8098f-d8b0-4721-bfce-70def1106d89'::uuid, '2026-10-07T11:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('6a2f1473-5df2-43d4-a3f2-9b12c5bdc624'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying consumer behavior in practice. The recent papers in our library on data mining would make a good companion read. The social context of consumer behavior is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-04T07:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9c13f51e-a27a-47a9-9fd6-58221fa532d4'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the understanding cyber law piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. We reproduced part of this for cyber law and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from fintech adoption; the overlap with understanding cyber law looks real.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-25T06:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e127101d-90a1-4ba1-aee4-7368b2ce5cf6'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the security piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper. In our group we used security on a small cyber law dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-19T23:03:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3645e814-dea5-4091-8869-8e16dc014bb8'::uuid, 'Good point, Arjun; I had not considered that angle on cyber law. A cleaner experiment might isolate understanding cyber law and keep everything else fixed.', '9c13f51e-a27a-47a9-9fd6-58221fa532d4'::uuid, '2026-07-26T13:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a079eb32-6c47-49d0-b235-8d5f47791a83'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of the paper is less the headline number and more how it handles understanding cyber law. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the security results? I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the cyber law results hold. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-20T04:58:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3eaf5094-5067-4445-b596-6f56fa2d1489'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the artificial intelligence regulation results hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-22T00:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('efcb966c-6b72-47a6-b4e4-df5c9d4ab823'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a engineering point of view. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from m ori versus simply more tuning. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-27T12:36:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('369f3791-20e6-41c7-b391-4906e918c568'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of artificial intelligence regulation keeps coming up in our seminars. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the artificial intelligence regulation results hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-24T10:58:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz)
