  ('abe80686-9404-485b-a15a-a7a0a6fde4aa'::uuid, 'Thanks Tanvi, that clarifies the m ori part for me.', 'efcb966c-6b72-47a6-b4e4-df5c9d4ab823'::uuid, '2026-10-29T02:22:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e40e8b5c-2e9a-4ec1-bd40-9f7116bb19ad'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying VLSI design in practice. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the VLSI design results hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-04T03:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b61c0ad0-a531-46d0-a7f5-63160cdb5594'::uuid, 'Building on Aditya''s comment, the VLSI design assumption matters a lot here. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from data privacy law; the overlap with VLSI design looks real. I would flag the privacy and public-policy implications of VLSI design before anyone builds on it.', 'e40e8b5c-2e9a-4ec1-bd40-9f7116bb19ad'::uuid, '2026-07-06T02:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('37498c3d-3977-477a-be76-b5d7abee56b6'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. A colleague''s project on VLSI design hit the same issue with VLSI design. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about VLSI design in the wild.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-01T02:23:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('cd9608be-d6f9-4252-b6ad-05231803eb73'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the do people accept public-policy question deserves more attention than it gets. Related reading: surveys on cyber law cover the background on integrative public-policy-acceptance framework nicely. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-21T11:41:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('37b7eaf9-a66d-4369-a142-35a279526b7c'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on public policy.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-12T00:08:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('847c5d5d-c999-4e49-9623-99f0acdbcb6a'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “When and Why Do People Accept Public-Policy Interventions? An…” is a useful lens on public policy. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about public policy in the wild. On our side the integrative public-policy-acceptance framework step was the bottleneck, not the main method.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-11T21:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('52fa8179-1533-45b4-9710-2b6f7eae9a12'::uuid, 'Agreed with Deepak on the main point. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for public policy.', '847c5d5d-c999-4e49-9623-99f0acdbcb6a'::uuid, '2026-07-13T06:04:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ba09c132-c551-41ce-af9a-6031403ba18c'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on public policy.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-12T07:48:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f5eeb9c6-c2cd-4992-b86b-cf077bab5de4'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of signal processing keeps coming up in our seminars. Did you check how it performs when the input around digital signal processing is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-21T20:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4b74de6a-41f6-4e1b-9c41-d82e1e7555e5'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying signal processing in practice. There is a useful parallel with data mining, where the role of digital signal processing is comparable.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-20T04:43:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('37cf3f46-ec45-48bd-aa0c-139a23262cb0'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on signal processing. From a management perspective, the interesting part is the cost-benefit: what would adopting signal processing change for a firm''s decisions? My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for signal processing. Keen to see follow-up results.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-17T00:02:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('54d367f6-7f69-4c39-8f90-af08eb8f0cc2'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Ramesh: the evidence for digital signal processing is thinner than it looks.', 'f5eeb9c6-c2cd-4992-b86b-cf077bab5de4'::uuid, '2026-08-24T16:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5665c50c-4704-4564-b30d-08ffff411e2b'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on CRISPR gene editing. How does this compare with last year''s work on supply chain analytics? The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of vectors.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-01T11:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c6ea9077-5220-4de4-b96c-579af37cc7f6'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around neurological disorders is easy to underestimate. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from sustainable finance; the overlap with vectors looks real.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-24T23:16:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('816d9c28-779f-40fb-8119-2349d5af2d2d'::uuid, 'Agreed with Aditya on the main point. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split. This connects to the work on embedded systems, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. Keen to see follow-up results.', '5665c50c-4704-4564-b30d-08ffff411e2b'::uuid, '2026-10-03T05:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('979cfbd6-20cd-4ac7-8bbd-501f953efa75'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Vectors in CRISPR Gene Editing for Neurological Disorders” is less the headline number and more how it handles neurological disorders. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around CRISPR gene editing easier to trust.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-02T01:15:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('37d941e7-bde2-4479-bd5b-90faad40d818'::uuid, 'Vikram, could you say more about how you handled vectors? The recent papers in our library on supply chain analytics would make a good companion read. It would help to see how neurological disorders performs for smaller organisations with limited data.', '816d9c28-779f-40fb-8119-2349d5af2d2d'::uuid, '2026-10-03T05:52:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('76699a49-1d49-43ed-904c-4deffcdda937'::uuid, 'I skimmed “REVIEWING THE IMPACT OF EMBEDDED SYSTEMS IN MEDICAL DEVICES…” last week, and the framing of MEDICAL DEVICES is the part I would discuss first. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of REVIEWING. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-21T04:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('38ace2ac-cceb-453c-b0b5-8a8e31c1ce19'::uuid, 'Meera, that matches my experience too. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding EMBEDDED SYSTEMS.', '76699a49-1d49-43ed-904c-4deffcdda937'::uuid, '2026-06-21T06:20:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('42618c03-944b-4c94-9b7e-32afef4d9ceb'::uuid, 'Helpful context, Meera. The recent papers in our library on wireless sensor networks would make a good companion read. Is there a public dataset we could use to test EMBEDDED SYSTEMS ourselves? I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', '76699a49-1d49-43ed-904c-4deffcdda937'::uuid, '2026-06-22T08:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e2bb81eb-f3d1-4373-9900-c5415a95dea9'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of embedded systems keeps coming up in our seminars. The recent papers in our library on artificial intelligence regulation would make a good companion read. How does this compare with last year''s work on artificial intelligence regulation?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-22T10:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bd6b40e2-ee31-44ec-b04b-476166984868'::uuid, 'Meera, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. There is a useful parallel with wireless sensor networks, where the role of EMBEDDED SYSTEMS is comparable. From an engineering angle, I would want to see how embedded systems behaves under distribution shift before relying on it. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', '76699a49-1d49-43ed-904c-4deffcdda937'::uuid, '2026-06-21T04:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
