  ('c45d2d64-77e7-42e0-ade0-0aeceb7813e6'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on computer vision. I would add a humanities lens: how research on computer vision is framed and interpreted matters as much as the technical result.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-24T15:41:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3a4c7143-5283-4eea-bb1c-44220a9ff706'::uuid, 'Agreed with Siddharth on the main point.', 'c45d2d64-77e7-42e0-ade0-0aeceb7813e6'::uuid, '2026-09-27T06:43:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3a783ef8-b65b-4975-9d7a-bcecc065fb0f'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on wireless sensor networks for a while, so I''m glad it came up. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about wireless sensor networks in the wild.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-09T01:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('6027fdfb-ff28-477a-a1c8-5f45ee61cd00'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. There is a useful parallel with computer vision, where the role of smart water quality monitoring is comparable. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for wireless sensor networks. Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-01T03:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('93ae0711-3700-4cd6-81e0-75ac8503f94b'::uuid, 'I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the wireless sensor networks results hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-08T11:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e3bf4e15-deb1-4ed8-b649-8b1d5b3596cb'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Fintech adoption, the regulatory environment and bank stability” is less the headline number and more how it handles bank stability. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of investigation. This connects to the work on public policy, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-06T12:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3b26c8f9-1337-4761-a6ab-f2d000ae8375'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around investigation is easy to underestimate. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say cognitive psychology?', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-04T00:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('471fb197-855e-455a-910c-8066d33237c3'::uuid, 'One option is to run a small ablation on VLSI design and share the numbers with the group.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-30T17:58:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3b41aac8-a274-4bd5-a885-2d31e89b6008'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper. Did you check how it performs when the input around VLSI design is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-04T21:33:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c1060ff8-c087-462f-b0e5-93fdbd4880d1'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Sunita: the evidence for VLSI design is thinner than it looks. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', '471fb197-855e-455a-910c-8066d33237c3'::uuid, '2026-07-02T06:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ab2c6374-7afd-4bcf-8cf4-c53ee67d0e11'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on cognitive psychology. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of cognitive psychology. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from fintech adoption; the overlap with cognitive psychology looks real. Keen to see follow-up results.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-28T00:20:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('be0a262c-70ed-4ccd-b97e-d556971d4144'::uuid, 'I skimmed “The future of cognitive psychology” last week, and the framing of cognitive psychology is the part I would discuss first. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-02T19:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3bcdc31e-1213-4277-ad0b-5e14c890e7b8'::uuid, 'Helpful context, Anjali. There is a useful parallel with sustainable finance, where the role of cognitive psychology is comparable. When we tried a similar setup for cognitive psychology, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did.', 'ab2c6374-7afd-4bcf-8cf4-c53ee67d0e11'::uuid, '2026-06-29T07:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('42882ddd-413a-4a5d-becc-3c42a308d151'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude. For context, the graph neural networks literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-25T12:20:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a35e33f3-4e3f-4a70-8301-425e55e33baa'::uuid, 'Building on Sunita''s comment, the analysis assumption matters a lot here. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for artificial intelligence regulation policies? Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude.', '42882ddd-413a-4a5d-becc-3c42a308d151'::uuid, '2026-07-26T03:32:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8672627d-fd00-4150-bfb0-3f345e764b83'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for artificial intelligence regulation policies? Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-24T15:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3be9ece8-9d70-487f-ac85-a5de252f4c5a'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying artificial intelligence regulation in practice. Did you check how it performs when the input around artificial intelligence regulation policies is noisy or partially missing? From a management perspective, the interesting part is the cost-benefit: what would adopting artificial intelligence regulation change for a firm''s decisions? I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-20T21:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a2b7a54d-5783-4ca3-80c5-cc37086e0f62'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. One option is to run a small ablation on artificial intelligence regulation policies and share the numbers with the group. The recent papers in our library on supply chain analytics would make a good companion read. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-26T08:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4d2bbacb-fb35-46db-aadf-8eda4a49fced'::uuid, 'Building on Rahul''s comment, the analysis assumption matters a lot here. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around artificial intelligence regulation easier to trust. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input.', '8672627d-fd00-4150-bfb0-3f345e764b83'::uuid, '2026-07-25T13:41:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a064dac9-0f82-436e-8d85-02511127b195'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a biosciences point of view.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-12T13:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('98648f16-67c5-4155-8ca8-3cdf00ebf4b7'::uuid, 'Priya, could you say more about how you handled early cancer detection? When we tried a similar setup for bioinformatics, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did.', 'a064dac9-0f82-436e-8d85-02511127b195'::uuid, '2026-10-14T05:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3c2b67f8-3441-49b4-a9bb-3e8baf37246b'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Sanya: the evidence for early cancer detection is thinner than it looks. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around bioinformatics easier to trust. A cleaner experiment might isolate early cancer detection and keep everything else fixed. I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', '98648f16-67c5-4155-8ca8-3cdf00ebf4b7'::uuid, '2026-10-16T08:04:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f3b4eae5-5993-4eca-b8f1-7f1602aba546'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on bioinformatics for a while, so I''m glad it came up. Before this informs experiments, we would need validation on independent samples for early cancer detection. A cleaner experiment might isolate early cancer detection and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-15T08:49:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('744fac51-dda3-4953-91c8-9b4265bc1f77'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on cyber law. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-28T13:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('7fcfd275-499e-444b-9714-a7c220939ce9'::uuid, 'Do the authors say anything about computational cost for cyber law cyber crimes?', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-23T04:27:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a47e1171-b8a2-495f-bb4a-ec28e4964324'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Shreya: the evidence for cyber law cyber crimes is thinner than it looks. There is a useful parallel with bioinformatics, where the role of cyber law cyber crimes is comparable.', '744fac51-dda3-4953-91c8-9b4265bc1f77'::uuid, '2026-08-30T04:10:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f46cccf7-4944-4dc1-addd-da7df2029b49'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Bhavana: the evidence for cyber law cyber crimes is thinner than it looks. Related reading: surveys on sustainable finance cover the background on cyber law cyber crimes nicely. Consider tracking cyber law cyber crimes separately so that regressions are easier to spot. Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', '7fcfd275-499e-444b-9714-a7c220939ce9'::uuid, '2026-08-24T00:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('da9900ca-486b-4d2a-9175-08a45eef99f7'::uuid, 'It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from cyber law cyber crimes versus simply more tuning.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-23T08:13:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3d173883-8caa-4b6a-9f5d-6ba543dae198'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Cyber Law & Cyber Crimes Simplified” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. Related reading: surveys on digital humanities cover the background on cyber law cyber crimes nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-28T09:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3d66eaa7-6223-46da-92c4-15c3f0e16f21'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. For context, the wireless sensor networks literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. When we tried a similar setup for computer vision, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-12T08:49:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('a86e50c6-a135-4d7f-9946-250d2c2e92d1'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Computer Vision” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. From a statistical point of view, I would want to see uncertainty estimates around the computer vision results, not only point values.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-18T02:00:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('afc0180b-dfd1-488a-bc5e-664ade69ab2a'::uuid, 'Thanks Bhavana, that clarifies the computer vision part for me. If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', 'a86e50c6-a135-4d7f-9946-250d2c2e92d1'::uuid, '2026-08-18T16:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('67a3e7f3-05c5-4b4a-9edd-c446bfdb725e'::uuid, 'Is there a public dataset we could use to test computer vision ourselves?', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-18T10:43:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('4a48c185-c6c3-47f0-b8d0-af90c8ffbc11'::uuid, 'Aishwarya, could you say more about how you handled computer vision? Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude. Did you check how it performs when the input around computer vision is noisy or partially missing?', 'afc0180b-dfd1-488a-bc5e-664ade69ab2a'::uuid, '2026-08-19T16:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('91a0d9c9-bf5b-4385-9397-3bb14e1786b7'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Neoliberalism Studies and Media Studies” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. One option is to run a small ablation on neoliberalism studies and share the numbers with the group. Public-facing claims about neoliberalism studies deserve careful wording, since non-specialists will read them very differently.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-26T01:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3d6b523e-fb3f-487c-aaf6-3033e4fc43de'::uuid, 'That is a fair summary, Harsh, but one detail about media studies is missing. How does this compare with last year''s work on data privacy law?', '91a0d9c9-bf5b-4385-9397-3bb14e1786b7'::uuid, '2026-07-28T15:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dd39fd0e-6c40-4b3c-ba02-d39755ee0fce'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the research question deserves more attention than it gets. I would flag the privacy and public-policy implications of research before anyone builds on it.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-12T22:24:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('60e6286b-b05a-4c93-a31e-46bd437500c6'::uuid, 'Thanks Gaurav, that clarifies the research part for me.', 'dd39fd0e-6c40-4b3c-ba02-d39755ee0fce'::uuid, '2026-09-13T10:22:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3d727490-148a-4f18-9903-1e84f3e98cc1'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the research question deserves more attention than it gets. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-19T23:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3d77db79-955f-42b5-9f4f-7f6f2c877535'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the structuration theory approach question deserves more attention than it gets. For context, the media studies literature has been debating a very similar question for some time.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-16T17:54:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ac0aa5ba-380e-4722-8d8d-19c2844b90cf'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. Did you check how it performs when the input around structuration theory approach is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-24T14:22:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('6abda339-0185-4a34-b137-7409ac5a91bb'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a humanities and social sciences point of view. We reproduced part of this for cyber law and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-22T00:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3da5c6eb-3e6f-4d8c-a4ab-5a7dae9cf33a'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around CYBER LAW is easy to underestimate. Is the code or the exact configuration available so we can reproduce the CYBER CRIME results? The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of CYBER LAW. Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-24T03:01:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dbbad654-b4f2-4fcf-8acb-ac79c9c4480a'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around CYBER LAW is easy to underestimate. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around cyber law easier to trust. The recent papers in our library on synthetic biology would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-22T20:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ec5fee87-a4c6-4497-aa74-9160bcb20875'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Wicked Problems in Public Policy” is less the headline number and more how it handles responding. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from supply chain analytics; the overlap with wicked problems looks real.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-12T01:36:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3dcf49c2-a2cf-4db3-a53e-d506fd1a3dd7'::uuid, 'Building on Faizan''s comment, the wicked problems assumption matters a lot here. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from fintech adoption; the overlap with understanding looks real.', 'ec5fee87-a4c6-4497-aa74-9160bcb20875'::uuid, '2026-11-14T23:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('cee19a1b-e6a9-4c87-bda2-50670bd3c89f'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the understanding question deserves more attention than it gets. How does this compare with last year''s work on signal processing? The recent papers in our library on signal processing would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-09T07:38:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e7d8e76c-a62d-468a-9f9b-7340d34107ec'::uuid, 'Agreed with Aditya on the main point. Is there a public dataset we could use to test wicked problems ourselves? The limitations section is thin, especially regarding responding.', '3dcf49c2-a2cf-4db3-a53e-d506fd1a3dd7'::uuid, '2026-11-14T23:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('48914f0c-04de-4714-94c0-ed0824758c5e'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Wicked Problems in Public Policy” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-14T15:26:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3e531a0b-8a67-4ddf-86a3-5b0b8a0b6f74'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on protein folding for a while, so I''m glad it came up. For context, the intellectual property literature has been debating a very similar question for some time. It would help to see how proteins fold performs for smaller organisations with limited data.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-21T22:15:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ab78f454-69bd-48d5-8c61-fe01ed87a1e5'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Decoding How Proteins Fold” is a useful lens on protein folding. The recent papers in our library on cyber law would make a good companion read. We reproduced part of this for protein folding and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-17T02:15:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d3cb2043-c060-4e23-9f40-d53850061505'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Decoding How Proteins Fold” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. Last semester''s reading group went through “Decoding How Proteins Fold”, and most of the debate centred on decoding. There is a useful parallel with cyber law, where the role of proteins fold is comparable.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-20T02:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('73c1b413-0711-4637-b324-8771dc847cc2'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. The recent papers in our library on cyber law would make a good companion read. In our group we used proteins fold on a small protein folding dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-24T05:43:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fbe8a2be-f4ec-4444-a264-f6960cb39be3'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on data mining for a while, so I''m glad it came up. The recent papers in our library on cyber law would make a good companion read. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-16T23:48:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('9ac9b6df-0981-43dd-8a2f-a98f31ae6582'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Kavya, though I think it depends on the dataset. There is a useful parallel with protein folding, where the role of agriculture is comparable. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding agriculture.', 'fbe8a2be-f4ec-4444-a264-f6960cb39be3'::uuid, '2026-09-19T13:02:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3ecb6a1c-a3cf-4ead-90a1-1f3f0ca801bd'::uuid, 'Kavya, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper.', 'fbe8a2be-f4ec-4444-a264-f6960cb39be3'::uuid, '2026-09-17T18:08:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ef5526c1-708b-4b3f-9539-4faef01dd864'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on data mining. From a legal standpoint, how agriculture is documented will matter if the results are ever challenged.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-18T21:23:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('3f321da7-2f0b-457c-8d6e-0611140ff115'::uuid, 'Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around artificial intelligence regulation easier to trust.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-23T05:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
