  ('8d58c66c-ddfe-4dc6-85b9-7f8887d7a5ea'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. The social context of protein folding is largely absent here, and I think it changes how we should read the findings. Has anyone compared this against a simple baseline for protein folding? Keen to see follow-up results.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-29T13:53:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8875bec6-7aa5-431b-b03a-ba9e9d510042'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the framework question deserves more attention than it gets. Last semester''s reading group went through “Solvent”, and most of the debate centred on solvent. There is a useful parallel with bioinformatics, where the role of framework is comparable.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-30T06:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('785ab70e-cbc0-4bc1-911d-e02dc8e4ef69'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. This connects to the work on computer vision, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. From a statistical point of view, I would want to see uncertainty estimates around the protein folding results, not only point values.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-23T01:08:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('8065ea29-2aea-472c-9c0f-709fe0023bad'::uuid, 'Thanks Deepak, that clarifies the framework part for me. It would help to state the assumptions behind solvent formally and check which of them actually hold. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of framework.', '6459f588-2f9d-4a78-a24f-2dc6ad1af1ac'::uuid, '2026-08-30T21:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('43c43306-f9b5-4379-a17c-f1abe21cf22f'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Pooja: the evidence for framework is thinner than it looks. Consider tracking solvent separately so that regressions are easier to spot. The recent papers in our library on CRISPR gene editing would make a good companion read. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', '8875bec6-7aa5-431b-b03a-ba9e9d510042'::uuid, '2026-08-30T11:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bc72ae7f-5fed-46c3-bb88-13e42edfc3e7'::uuid, 'I skimmed “DATA PRIVACY LAWS AND COMPLIANCE” last week, and the framing of EU GDPR is the part I would discuss first. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for DATA PRIVACY LAWS?', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-07T08:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('448116bb-7c09-4c0a-b49f-cd1f170738a3'::uuid, 'Deepak, that matches my experience too. It would be worth asking whose perspective is missing from the data behind COMPARATIVE. If you are open to it, we could draft a short comparison note for the reading group.', 'bc72ae7f-5fed-46c3-bb88-13e42edfc3e7'::uuid, '2026-08-08T05:00:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dd764112-3f80-4952-89fb-fad5e93f957b'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. Did you check how it performs when the input around DATA PRIVACY LAWS is noisy or partially missing? In our group we used COMPLIANCE on a small data privacy law dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-03T00:54:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
