  ('50976a01-5732-4f38-9f25-21c496cdb207'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on digital humanities for a while, so I''m glad it came up. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for digital humanities. This connects to the work on computer vision, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-05T06:13:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('5142ba4a-6772-486a-a14f-f518cb021e32'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on data privacy law. From a statistical point of view, I would want to see uncertainty estimates around the data privacy law results, not only point values.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-26T23:42:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('51e3571a-b074-47ac-8f1c-d0e187648c00'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the gene editing s future piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from gene editing s future versus simply more tuning.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-11T05:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e275d7fb-f31c-4666-97e1-5a599085c6eb'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on CRISPR gene editing for a while, so I''m glad it came up. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say protein folding? The limitations section is thin, especially regarding gene editing s future.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-12T17:21:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fd99ee62-4f0f-4991-9917-3201787be501'::uuid, 'I skimmed “Reviewing the Role of AI and Machine Learning in…” last week, and the framing of machine learning is the part I would discuss first. The recent papers in our library on fintech adoption would make a good companion read.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-08T05:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('521e0be7-d986-4e79-94c3-0837618a9137'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the reviewing question deserves more attention than it gets. Did you check how it performs when the input around machine learning is noisy or partially missing? There is a useful parallel with cyber law, where the role of reviewing is comparable. Sharing a few references in the group folder later this week.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-11T06:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz)
