  ('b997e2ab-3b1e-420f-8fee-bb97687dd103'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-15T07:37:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bf7ab9d9-9e86-4c32-8cb3-401c684973f2'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. I would flag the privacy and public-policy implications of cybersecurity before anyone builds on it. We reproduced part of this for data mining and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-07T19:05:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f3df27d7-5f5f-40e4-a2f4-b53193951816'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the data mining techniques piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. When we tried a similar setup for data mining, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did. For context, the digital humanities literature has been debating a very similar question for some time.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-14T11:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f89e9c84-2106-477d-85f0-9367678f631e'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. This connects to the work on VLSI design, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-08T08:23:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('baa72585-37da-497e-9de4-8273a22073a0'::uuid, 'Appreciate you sharing this with the group. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about data mining in the wild.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-14T10:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ab394c4e-0f2f-4074-819c-a772b8a413da'::uuid, 'Building on Priya''s comment, the data mining assumption matters a lot here. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the data mining results hold.', 'f89e9c84-2106-477d-85f0-9367678f631e'::uuid, '2026-11-10T12:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ac7455af-38fa-4398-92ba-10a88a25ce23'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Data Mining for Predictive Analytics” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. Did you check how it performs when the input around predictive analytics is noisy or partially missing? The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of predictive analytics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-03T21:47:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ad774e3a-9d1d-4bfb-b134-857b19c76eaf'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of sustainable finance keeps coming up in our seminars. From a statistical point of view, I would want to see uncertainty estimates around the sustainable finance results, not only point values.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-27T14:46:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fe0b122b-1684-4cd5-a11c-a48f22775876'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Anjali, though I think it depends on the dataset.', 'ad774e3a-9d1d-4bfb-b134-857b19c76eaf'::uuid, '2026-06-28T00:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f08c1566-4a41-40fb-9362-8289941a7369'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Sustainable Finance in Emerging Markets” is a useful lens on sustainable finance. When we tried a similar setup for sustainable finance, preprocessing choices changed the outcome more than the model did. From a legal standpoint, how emerging markets is documented will matter if the results are ever challenged. Keen to see follow-up results.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-22T21:57:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dc80cc8e-32b8-4d73-9ab5-e9552ffcba35'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Sustainable Finance in Emerging Markets” is less the headline number and more how it handles emerging markets. A sensitivity analysis would show how stable the conclusions about sustainable finance are to small changes in the data.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-21T03:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bee66ebf-790b-4847-9938-95fd1efa3347'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on CRISPR gene editing for a while, so I''m glad it came up. The recent papers in our library on digital humanities would make a good companion read. For wet-lab collaborators, the useful question is whether the CRISPR gene editing results survive biological replicates rather than a single benchmark.', NULL::uuid, '2026-05-27T10:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e70e57b8-8506-45a0-aad6-cf23d736d567'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of CRISPR gene editing keeps coming up in our seminars. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the CRISPR gene editing results hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-05-31T01:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ad843015-7183-4a4b-b6dd-b26a41c96d92'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “CRISPR gene editing” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. It would be worth asking whose perspective is missing from the data behind moving closer. Scalability is the open question; it is unclear how this behaves when the data grows by an order of magnitude. Happy to share my notes if that helps.', NULL::uuid, '2026-05-27T11:19:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('aebe9087-060e-4241-89a7-1b375ad1ac2a'::uuid, 'Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around supply chain analytics easier to trust.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-02T02:43:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fd5437b9-d3b4-4306-aa61-dc8e800452c8'::uuid, 'I skimmed “Benefits of Deploying Supply Chain Analytics” last week, and the framing of deploying supply chain analytics is the part I would discuss first. On our side the benefits step was the bottleneck, not the main method.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-06T20:26:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b114a6e6-1ac5-4583-844a-e904190c2f1a'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on synthetic biology. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding biomaterial design. Related reading: surveys on cyber law cover the background on living interface nicely.', NULL::uuid, '2026-08-25T06:01:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b5327632-acc7-442e-8382-762b985cec1b'::uuid, 'A cleaner experiment might isolate cognitive psychology and keep everything else fixed.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-01T20:14:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ef3932a0-62a5-48b7-b060-91cac83f3b2b'::uuid, 'Suresh, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. One option is to run a small ablation on cognitive psychology and share the numbers with the group. How does this compare with last year''s work on signal processing? Looking forward to hearing what others think.', 'b5327632-acc7-442e-8382-762b985cec1b'::uuid, '2026-06-03T06:16:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f7ea611e-b7ce-4edd-acfa-b81468c4f7e9'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Suresh, though I think it depends on the dataset. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one? The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of cognitive psychology.', 'b5327632-acc7-442e-8382-762b985cec1b'::uuid, '2026-06-03T08:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e0b07148-9788-4ab5-9e4d-42b723835180'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Cognitive Psychology” is a useful lens on cognitive psychology. I would flag the privacy and public-policy implications of cognitive psychology before anyone builds on it. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say cyber law?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-03T00:18:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b7c0e6a3-c343-4256-9b02-ebd82f3247b6'::uuid, 'Worth a closer look when we plan the next computer vision project.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-05T15:13:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d2f728bc-826b-4945-8a09-645a12d496c0'::uuid, 'Lakshmi, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. Reporting confidence intervals would make the claims around computer vision easier to trust. On the hardware side, any computer vision pipeline would have to fit a tight power and latency budget, so I would profile it on a real board. I would be glad to discuss this at the next group meeting.', 'b7c0e6a3-c343-4256-9b02-ebd82f3247b6'::uuid, '2026-11-05T17:30:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('b7e9f2f1-1e0d-4a96-a2cd-83111b6b3d5e'::uuid, 'Nice find, and a good reminder that the transdisciplinarity question deserves more attention than it gets. From a legal standpoint, how transdisciplinarity is documented will matter if the results are ever challenged.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-09T14:10:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('fd5b018a-b5f0-46e1-9925-21c3227b1ad9'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “Transdisciplinarity and public policy” is less the headline number and more how it handles transdisciplinarity. In our group we used transdisciplinarity on a small public policy dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from cyber law; the overlap with transdisciplinarity looks real.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-12T10:00:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d281ca2e-10b6-44d6-8214-3e7568d1ffbd'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around transdisciplinarity is easy to underestimate. Related reading: surveys on sustainable finance cover the background on transdisciplinarity nicely. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-10T07:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ba837787-726c-433f-ac41-8e2d4e06c925'::uuid, 'I skimmed “Protein Folding and Structure” last week, and the framing of structure is the part I would discuss first. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper. We saw noticeable sensitivity to random seeds, so I would report results over several runs.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-04T10:56:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bba4fc0e-7f78-41db-b54a-5bed1f69e223'::uuid, 'Quick note before the details: I''m reading this mostly from a humanities and social sciences point of view. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters? In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input. Looking forward to hearing what others think.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-06T18:26:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('cfda3587-d1f4-4d86-9c52-de5f114288b9'::uuid, 'I tried reproducing a small part of this and had mixed results. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for tourism?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-07T18:25:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d883620a-c31d-475f-a049-0bf6d2f9bc84'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on cognitive psychology for a while, so I''m glad it came up. The limitations section is thin, especially regarding tourism. For context, the wireless sensor networks literature has been debating a very similar question for some time.', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-04T02:29:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('bc18c12c-79fe-4ac3-97ed-cc3794ffe39f'::uuid, 'Do the authors say anything about computational cost for strategic supply chain analytics?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-27T20:35:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c8051b1c-4fdc-43f8-9467-c7355379a3ad'::uuid, 'Agreed with Aishwarya on the main point. In our group we used strategic supply chain analytics on a small supply chain analytics dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent. Did you check how it performs when the input around strategic supply chain analytics is noisy or partially missing? Happy to share my notes if that helps.', 'bc18c12c-79fe-4ac3-97ed-cc3794ffe39f'::uuid, '2026-06-30T14:55:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c1bc3e2f-8e7f-4bae-813d-7c471312c85c'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on synthetic biology for a while, so I''m glad it came up. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the synthetic biology results hold. Did you check how it performs when the input around applications is noisy or partially missing?', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-27T04:46:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d536c223-8ce8-46e2-b71d-cf7395f2b09b'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying synthetic biology in practice. Several of the reported gains are small enough that they could disappear under a different split. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say artificial intelligence regulation?', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-20T16:04:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('f6c366ee-92cb-41d5-be46-06ae1a78571e'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Harsh: the evidence for classification is thinner than it looks.', 'd536c223-8ce8-46e2-b71d-cf7395f2b09b'::uuid, '2026-09-20T18:56:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c7e52fce-570d-423b-824e-d36f168c870d'::uuid, 'Interesting thread. My first reaction is that the trustllm piece is doing most of the heavy lifting here. It is not clear how much of the improvement comes from trustworthiness versus simply more tuning. It may help to add a qualitative error analysis alongside the headline metrics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-07T16:26:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('efca6459-742a-48d1-82c2-b70268c0b683'::uuid, 'I would gently disagree, Tanvi: the evidence for trustllm is thinner than it looks. One option is to run a small ablation on trustworthiness and share the numbers with the group. This connects to the work on fintech adoption, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. I will revisit this after I have had time to run a few experiments.', 'c7e52fce-570d-423b-824e-d36f168c870d'::uuid, '2026-07-10T14:17:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c8001f5f-c649-49e6-a597-2b57cb0d27b2'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. It could be worth pairing this with ideas from CRISPR gene editing; the overlap with deep learning looks real. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-26T13:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('c805bef5-c573-4b09-a52e-f39239184cdb'::uuid, 'Short answer from my side: it depends heavily on the data you start with. Last semester''s reading group went through “Introduction to Bioinformatics”, and most of the debate centred on bioinformatics.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-21T01:00:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e3d1c023-15b3-48cf-8735-5e4ee8cd1ed3'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; “Computer Vision” is a useful lens on computer vision. In our group we used computer vision on a small computer vision dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-22T01:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ce1747b8-93eb-4fa4-b4d5-5ac8063da3aa'::uuid, 'Good question. I read “Computer Vision” a few weeks ago and it has stayed with me. In our group we used computer vision on a small computer vision dataset, and the gains were modest but consistent. Do the authors say anything about computational cost for computer vision?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-15T21:06:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ce3b8ada-eb33-49b2-9a60-f885cd945ed7'::uuid, 'This lines up with what we have seen when applying intellectual property in practice. On our side the intellectual property step was the bottleneck, not the main method. I worry the benchmark is too close to the training setup to say much about intellectual property in the wild.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-16T20:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d3597edc-09aa-490a-8002-811fb4216e91'::uuid, 'That is a fair summary, Imran, but one detail about intellectual property is missing. The comparison would be more convincing with a stronger baseline and a proper ablation of intellectual property. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', 'ce3b8ada-eb33-49b2-9a60-f885cd945ed7'::uuid, '2026-09-17T09:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ef725857-f7e9-4206-a260-6b00802b7759'::uuid, 'This is a timely question, and we ran into something similar while working on digital humanities. There is a useful parallel with cyber law, where the role of libraries is comparable.', NULL::uuid, '2026-11-01T00:44:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d5264c89-f361-4718-bf8d-591c0225e09f'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of digital humanities keeps coming up in our seminars. What would it take to adapt this to a different domain, say cognitive psychology?', NULL::uuid, '2026-10-27T12:12:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('d9018d5d-3c5c-413d-b472-94b4760218aa'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of embedded systems keeps coming up in our seminars. My main concern is whether the evaluation reflects realistic conditions for embedded systems. I would suggest a pilot on a small subset first, then scale up if the embedded systems results hold.', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-27T14:40:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('eade3e7e-6d62-4dc7-b77c-bd3daabe2686'::uuid, 'Honest take: the results look promising, but I would hold off on strong conclusions. The recent papers in our library on supply chain analytics would make a good companion read. Last semester''s reading group went through “NETWORKING WITH EMBEDDED SYSTEMS”, and most of the debate centred on NETWORKING.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-08T03:43:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dbfb65bf-2521-4ba9-bd0a-c3ed4ae0777e'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of “A Survey on Underwater Computer Vision” is less the headline number and more how it handles underwater computer vision. This connects to the work on large language models, which tackles a similar trade-off from a different direction. In a small pilot, the approach worked well on clean data and degraded quickly on messy real-world input. Let me know if a joint write-up would be useful.', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-14T09:04:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e55eb289-bc67-48be-ab4d-56b5a4d1efc5'::uuid, 'I think the interesting part of the paper is less the headline number and more how it handles methods. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-24T00:33:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('ed897db5-aeb6-4bdb-b629-080fa175d8f8'::uuid, 'Thanks for pushing on this, Mallika; I''ll report back once I have numbers for methods. We reproduced part of this for bioinformatics and the trend held, although the absolute numbers were lower.', 'e55eb289-bc67-48be-ab4d-56b5a4d1efc5'::uuid, '2026-07-24T05:24:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dd2f09ea-b5ea-4dd9-aed1-47da5e51aaa9'::uuid, 'Great discussion starter; the core idea around applications is easy to underestimate. From a management perspective, the interesting part is the cost-benefit: what would adopting bioinformatics change for a firm''s decisions? Our lab has been collecting notes on methods; the picture is more nuanced than the abstract suggests.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-20T15:23:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e3a8d257-3b4a-42ce-9376-06dd0f143d05'::uuid, 'I have been following this line of work on data mining for a while, so I''m glad it came up. Which metric did you prioritise, and does the ranking change if you pick another one?', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-07T02:31:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('efd28969-b2a4-4cf8-935b-edb1f63e5ab9'::uuid, 'Fair objection, Dev, though I think it depends on the dataset.', 'e3a8d257-3b4a-42ce-9376-06dd0f143d05'::uuid, '2026-07-09T23:59:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dfa53ab9-d70c-4720-b3cd-5bacdd0d8c45'::uuid, 'Mallika, this is the kind of detail that rarely makes it into the paper. Public-facing claims about web search deserve careful wording, since non-specialists will read them very differently. Related reading: surveys on public policy cover the background on proceedings nicely.', 'efd28969-b2a4-4cf8-935b-edb1f63e5ab9'::uuid, '2026-07-10T02:51:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('dd734df7-1695-4610-92b9-fd2ae2649a3d'::uuid, 'Worth discussing properly, because the topic of data mining keeps coming up in our seminars. How does this compare with last year''s work on cognitive psychology?', NULL::uuid, '2026-06-30T19:43:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e07a8897-1f84-47b7-8a1d-32d47db4a720'::uuid, 'I skimmed “The interplay of perceived benefit, perceived risk, and trust…” last week, and the framing of perceived benefit is the part I would discuss first. I would be cautious about generalising beyond the datasets reported in the paper.', NULL::uuid, '2026-07-15T03:46:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz),
  ('e25077df-5596-41cd-955a-b743edcf9086'::uuid, 'Thanks for bringing this up; the paper is a useful lens on supply chain analytics. How sensitive is it to the choice of hyperparameters?', NULL::uuid, '2026-09-21T19:45:02.127571+00:00'::timestamptz::timestamptz)
